{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c355","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a1832d-22a7-7bd3-b4f8-0a937add9938"},"sequence":5,"recorded_at":1780531400000005,"record_type":"status","durability":"ephemeral","causation_id":"01a1832d-2557-7c22-bf4d-f6336f6f7b2d","payload_type":"turn.input.user","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"command_id":"01a1832d-2557-7c22-bf4d-f6336f6f7b2d","kind":"turn_input_user","prompt":"Task 40 follow-up (small). Modal has no L4 capacity right now and narrate calls sit \"waiting to be scheduled\" for >10 min.\n\n1. pipeline/modal/narrate.py: change `gpu=\"L4\"` to a fallback list `gpu=[\"L4\", \"A10G\", \"T4\"]` (Modal tries them in order). Nothing else in that decorator.\n2. core/narration.ts: the per-second rate used for spend caps must stay conservative across that list. Rename KOKORO_L4_USD_PER_SEC to KOKORO_GPU_USD_PER_SEC = 0.000306 (A10G, about USD 1.10/h, the most expensive of the three) and update its comment; update all callers and tests.\n3. docs/contracts/narration.md: one sentence noting the GPU fallback list and that caps use the A10G rate.\nKeep the diff tiny. Run npm test and npm run typecheck. Commit with a clear message (the hook adds the co-author trailer). Do not run next start.","run_stream":{"id":"01a1832d-2557-7c22-bf4d-f6336f6f7b2d","kind":"run"}}}
