{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c39f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a1832d-22a7-7bd3-b4f8-0a937add9938"},"sequence":42,"recorded_at":1780531400000079,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"01a1832d-2557-7c22-bf4d-f6336f6f7b2d","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"command_id":"01a1832d-2557-7c22-bf4d-f6336f6f7b2d","event":{"chunk":"Read text file `docs/contracts/narration.md`.\n1|# Narration\n2|\n3|Read-aloud narration, one compact mp3 per chapter plus a per-chapter\n4|manifest with sentence timings. The unit is the chapter (owner\n5|decision): the reader plays any scene by seeking to its first sentence\n6|(`sceneSpan`) and highlights the sentence being read (`activeChunkAt`).\n7|Voice Kokoro-82M `af_heart` at speed 0.95, generated on a Modal GPU\n8|function that scales to zero.\n9|\n10|## Manifest\n11|\n12|`ChapterNarration` in `core/narration.ts`: `format: 2`, `key`, `src`,\n13|`durationSec`, `voice`, `model`, `speed`, and `chunks` with `n`\n14|(paragraph ordinal), `start`/`end` (char offsets into the paragraph),\n15|`t0`/`t1` (seconds), and `w` (word timings, below).\n16|`parseChapterNarration` throws on any bad field: it is a trust\n17|boundary, since the reader fetches this JSON. `src` is an `https:`\n18|URL or a same-origin path under `/narration/`.\n19|\n20|## Word timings\n21|\n22|No forced alignment: the Modal function returns each Kokoro token\n23|timestamp with chapter-absolute seconds per span, and `alignWords`\n24|maps them onto display words (`/[\\p{L}\\p{N}]+(?:['’][\\p{L}\\p{N}]+)*/u`,\n25|so \"Oz’s\" and \"didn't\" are one word and punctuation never\n26|highlights). Both sides compare on NFKD lowercase letters and digits\n27|with apostrophes dropped, in order with a lookahead of 3 either way;\n28|a token spanning several display words (\"well-known\") splits its time\n29|by character length. Words left without time interpolate between\n30|their neighbours; all times are clamped to the span and monotonic.\n31|`w` is flat `[start, end, t0, t1, ...]` with paragraph-relative char\n32|offsets and seconds, validated (multiple of 4, offsets in range,\n33|times in range, sorted) and required. `activeWordAt` drives the\n34|highlight, `wordAt` drives click-to-seek. Cost: 4 numbers per word,\n35|about 25 KB per chapter manifest.\n36|\n37|## Cache key\n38|\n39|`narrationKeyInput` builds a canonical string from the\n40|NFC-normalized, whitespace-collapsed chunk texts joined with `\"\\n\"`,\n41|plus voice, model, speed, and format. Callers hash it with SHA-256;\n42|`narrationKey` returns `narration/v2/<voice>/<first 32 hex>`. Same\n43|text + voice + model + speed gives the same key, any edit gives a new\n44|one. Audio lives at `<key>.mp3`, the manifest at `<key>.json`, as\n45|deterministic public Blob paths; the Redis index `narr:idx:<key>`\n46|holds the manifest JSON. Oz is pregenerated through the same keys, so\n47|a second reader of the same text gets it free.\n48|\n49|## Concurrency\n50|\n51|One reusable function, `ensureChapterNarration` in\n52|`core/narration-cache.ts`, serves the offline Oz run and the future\n53|upload route: index hit, then store hit with index backfill, then lock\n54|`narr:lock:<key>` (TTL 300 s, `setNxEx`; a null acquire means\n55|`pending`), one index re-check, budget reserve, synthesize, put audio\n56|and manifest, index set, release. Cache hits never touch the lock or\n57|the budget; failures refund once and release. No error text leaves the\n58|function.\n59|\n60|## Spend\n61|\n62|Integer micro-dollars. `estimateNarrationMicro(chars)` reserves the\n63|cap before generating: about 15 chars of audio per second, GPU time\n64|about 2% of audio after encode, plus 8 s of cold start/overhead, at\n65|the Modal L4 rate (`KOKORO_L4_USD_PER_SEC`, about USD 0.80/h). The\n66|server reserves on both the global spend key and the daily spend key\n67|(`spendKey()`, `dailySpendKey(day)` from `core/images`), refunding\n68|both past either cap; the global `DAILY_SPEND_CAP_USD` applies. The\n69|offline run caps with `NARRATION_CAP_USD` (default 2) and stops with a\n70|report instead of spending more. Worked number: an average Oz chapter\n71|of ~9,000 chars is about 10 min of audio, about 20 s of warm GPU,\n72|about USD 0.004.\n73|\n74|## Rolling window\n75|\n76|The owner warms two chapters ahead: at upload, chapters 1 and 2 while\n77|the book is processed; entering chapter N ensures N+1 and N+2; jumping\n78|to N ensures N and N+1. `chaptersToPrepare` in `core/narration.ts`\n79|computes the window; the client asks, the server dedupes through the\n80|index and lock.\n81|\n82|## Cold start\n83|\n84|About 15–30 s for the first chapter after the function scaled to zero\n85|(`scaledown_window=60`), warm calls a few seconds per chapter. The\n86|2-ahead window hides it after chapter 1. While a chapter is pending,\n87|the Read aloud control shows a quiet \"Getting the voice ready…\"\n88|state.\n89|\n90|## Operations\n91|\n92|Deploy with `modal deploy pipeline/modal/narrate.py`; the app\n93|`lectoria-narration` scales to zero a minute after the last call, and\n94|`modal app stop lectoria-narration` removes it entirely.\n95|\n96|## Open items\n97|\n98|Upload route wiring (uses `server/narration/cache.ts`, no route yet);\n99|Blob vs `public/` for Oz (same keys either way, so switching is a\n100|re-run).","final_result":true,"kind":"output","task_id":"01a1832d-2ed3-7ef3-8738-4b28df824958"},"kind":"task_lifecycle","run_stream":{"id":"01a1832d-2557-7c22-bf4d-f6336f6f7b2d","kind":"run"},"task_id":"01a1832d-2ed3-7ef3-8738-4b28df824958","task_stream":{"id":"01a1832d-2ed3-7ef3-8738-4b28df824958","kind":"task"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c3a1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a1832d-22a7-7bd3-b4f8-0a937add9938"},"sequence":43,"recorded_at":1780531400000081,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"01a1832d-2557-7c22-bf4d-f6336f6f7b2d","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"command_id":"01a1832d-2557-7c22-bf4d-f6336f6f7b2d","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a1832d-2ed3-7ef3-8738-4b28df824958"},"kind":"task_lifecycle","run_stream":{"id":"01a1832d-2557-7c22-bf4d-f6336f6f7b2d","kind":"run"},"task_id":"01a1832d-2ed3-7ef3-8738-4b28df824958","task_stream":{"id":"01a1832d-2ed3-7ef3-8738-4b28df824958","kind":"task"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c3a3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a1832d-22a7-7bd3-b4f8-0a937add9938"},"sequence":44,"recorded_at":1780531400000083,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"01a1832d-2557-7c22-bf4d-f6336f6f7b2d","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"command_id":"01a1832d-2557-7c22-bf4d-f6336f6f7b2d","event":{"chunk":"Read text file `pipeline/modal/narrate.py`.\n1|# Chapter narration on a Modal GPU: Kokoro-82M voice af_heart at 0.95x.\n2|# One function, narrate(texts, gaps, voice, speed), scales to zero after\n3|# a minute idle. Deploy with: modal deploy pipeline/modal/narrate.py.\n4|# Remove entirely with: modal app stop lectoria-narration.\n5|from __future__ import annotations\n6|\n7|import io\n8|import re\n9|import subprocess\n10|import tempfile\n11|import time\n12|\n13|import modal\n14|\n15|kimg = (\n16|    modal.Image.debian_slim(python_version=\"3.11\")\n17|    .apt_install(\"espeak-ng\", \"ffmpeg\")\n18|    .pip_install(\"kokoro==0.9.4\", \"soundfile\", \"numpy\", \"torch==2.5.1\", \"transformers==4.46.3\")\n19|)\n20|with kimg.imports():\n21|    import numpy as np\n22|    import soundfile as sf\n23|vol = modal.Volume.from_name(\"lectoria-hf-cache\", create_if_missing=True)\n24|app = modal.App(\"lectoria-narration\", image=kimg)\n25|\n26|SAMPLE_RATE = 24000\n27|MIN_SPAN_SAMPLES = int(round(0.05 * SAMPLE_RATE))\n28|VOICE_RE = re.compile(r\"^[a-z]{2}_[a-z]+$\")\n29|\n30|_pipe = None\n31|\n32|\n33|def pipeline():\n34|    global _pipe\n35|    if _pipe is None:\n36|        from kokoro import KPipeline\n37|\n38|        _pipe = KPipeline(lang_code=\"a\")\n39|    return _pipe\n40|\n41|\n42|def clean(text: str) -> str:\n43|    # Light TTS-only cleanup; offsets in the manifest never change because\n44|    # the caller keeps the original text for timing and display. Em dashes\n45|    # stay: Kokoro reads them fine and the tokens must match the display.\n46|    return text.replace(\"_\", \"\")\n47|\n48|\n49|WORD_RE = re.compile(r\"[^\\W_]\", re.UNICODE)\n50|\n51|\n52|def result_parts(result):\n53|    \"\"\"(audio samples, tokens) from one KPipeline result.\n54|\n55|    Real results are objects with .audio/.tokens; a plain\n56|    (graphemes, phonemes, audio) tuple yields audio with no tokens.\n57|    \"\"\"\n58|    audio = getattr(result, \"audio\", None)\n59|    tokens = getattr(result, \"tokens\", None)\n60|    if audio is None and isinstance(result, (tuple, list)):\n61|        audio = result[2] if len(result) > 2 else None\n62|        tokens = []\n63|    return np.asarray(audio, dtype=np.float32).reshape(-1), tokens or []\n64|\n65|\n66|def token_parts(token):\n67|    \"\"\"(text, start_ts, end_ts) from one token, object or sequence form.\"\"\"\n68|    if isinstance(token, (tuple, list)):\n69|        return token[0], token[2], token[3]\n70|    return token.text, token.start_ts, token.end_ts\n71|\n72|\n73|def check(texts, gaps, voice, speed):\n74|    if not isinstance(texts, list) or not 1 <= len(texts) <= 2000:\n75|        raise ValueError(\"texts must be a list of 1..2000 strings\")\n76|    if not isinstance(gaps, list) or len(gaps) != len(texts):\n77|        raise ValueError(\"gaps must match texts in length\")\n78|    for text in texts:\n79|        if not isinstance(text, str) or not 1 <= len(text) <= 2000:\n80|            raise ValueError(\"each text must be 1..2000 chars\")\n81|    for gap in gaps:\n82|        if not isinstance(gap, (int, float)) or not 0 <= gap <= 3:\n83|            raise ValueError(\"each gap must be 0..3 s\")\n84|    if not isinstance(voice, str) or not VOICE_RE.match(voice):\n85|        raise ValueError(\"voice must match ^[a-z]{2}_[a-z]+$\")\n86|    if not isinstance(speed, (int, float)) or not 0.5 <= speed <= 1.5:\n87|        raise ValueError(\"speed must be 0.5..1.5\")\n88|\n89|\n90|@app.function(gpu=\"L4\", scaledown_window=60, timeout=600, max_containers=4, volumes={\"/root/.cache/huggingface\": vol})\n91|def narrate(texts: list[str], gaps: list[float], voice: str, speed: float) -> dict:\n92|    started = time.monotonic()\n93|    check(texts, gaps, voice, speed)\n94|    pipe = pipeline()\n95|    parts: list[np.ndarray] = []\n96|    spans: list[dict] = []\n97|    cursor = 0\n98|    for text, gap in zip(texts, gaps):\n99|        t0 = cursor / SAMPLE_RATE\n100|        chunks = []\n101|        words: list = []\n102|        offset = 0\n103|        for result in pipe(clean(text), voice=voice, speed=float(speed)):\n104|            speech_chunk, tokens = result_parts(result)\n105|            # A result's audio offset inside the sentence is the running\n106|            # sample count of the results before it.\n107|            base = t0 + offset / SAMPLE_RATE\n108|            for token in tokens:\n109|                tok_text, start_ts, end_ts = token_parts(token)\n110|                if start_ts is None or end_ts is None:\n111|                    continue\n112|                if not WORD_RE.search(tok_text):\n113|                    continue\n114|                words.append([tok_text, round(base + float(start_ts), 3), round(base + float(end_ts), 3)])\n115|            chunks.append(speech_chunk)\n116|            offset += speech_chunk.shape[0]\n117|        speech = np.concatenate(chunks) if chunks else np.zeros(0, dtype=np.float32)\n118|        if speech.shape[0] < MIN_SPAN_SAMPLES:\n119|            # Kokoro can render a sentence as no audio (\"…\"); t0 == t1\n120|            # fails parseChapterNarration, so pad to a 50 ms floor.\n121|            speech = np.concatenate([speech, np.zeros(MIN_SPAN_SAMPLES - speech.shape[0], dtype=np.float32)])\n122|        parts.append(speech)\n123|        cursor += speech.shape[0]\n124|        spans.append({\"t0\": t0, \"t1\": cursor / SAMPLE_RATE, \"words\": words})\n125|        silence = int(round(float(gap) * SAMPLE_RATE))\n126|        if silence > 0:\n127|            parts.append(np.zeros(silence, dtype=np.float32))\n128|            cursor += silence\n129|    full = np.concatenate(parts) if parts else np.zeros(0, dtype=np.float32)\n130|    with tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(suffix=\".wav\") as wav, tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(suffix=\".mp3\") as mp3:\n131|        sf.write(wav.name, full, SAMPLE_RATE)\n132|        subprocess.run(\n133|            [\"ffmpeg\", \"-y\", \"-v\", \"error\", \"-i\", wav.name, \"-ac\", \"1\", \"-ar\", \"24000\", \"-b:a\", \"32k\", \"-codec:a\", \"libmp3lame\", mp3.name],\n134|            check=True,\n135|        )\n136|        mp3_bytes = open(mp3.name, \"rb\").read()\n137|    return {\n138|        \"mp3\": mp3_bytes,\n139|        \"durationSec\": cursor / SAMPLE_RATE,\n140|        \"spans\": spans,\n141|        \"gpuSec\": time.monotonic() - started,\n142|    }","final_result":true,"kind":"output","task_id":"01a1832d-2ec4-7832-9257-02358d6460fa"},"kind":"task_lifecycle","run_stream":{"id":"01a1832d-2557-7c22-bf4d-f6336f6f7b2d","kind":"run"},"task_id":"01a1832d-2ec4-7832-9257-02358d6460fa","task_stream":{"id":"01a1832d-2ec4-7832-9257-02358d6460fa","kind":"task"}}}
