l from `actualNarrationMicro(gpuSec)` summed). Print one line per chapter (`ch 3: generated 412.5 s audio, 7.1 s gpu` or `ch 3: cached`) and a cost summary.\\n- `build.ts`: `--step narrate` creates the Kokoro client lazily only when the step runs; `--dry-run` covers it. Narration needs neither META_API_KEY nor JEV_API_KEY.\\n- Tests for runNarrate with a fake synthesize and a temp dir: writes manifests for every chapter, second run is all cached with zero cost, cap refusal stops spending.\\n\\n## 5. Server cache adapters `server/narration/cache.ts` (no route yet)\\n`import \\\"server-only\\\"`. `createNarrationDeps({ kv, env, synthesize })` returning NarrationDeps for the future upload route: index in Redis under `narr:idx:<key>` (JSON, validated with parseChapterNarration on read), lock `narr:lock:<key>` via `kv.setNxEx(…, token, 300)` and `kv.releaseIfToken`, Blob store as above (server version), budget reserving on BOTH the global spend key and the daily spend key from core/images (`spendKey()`, `dailySpendKey(day)`) against `env.spendCapMicro` / `env.dailySpendCapMicro`, refunding both if either cap is passed (same pattern as server/images/orchestrate.ts). A BYOK path is not part of narration (narration always uses our Modal credits). Plus `server/narration/kokoro.ts` = `import \\\"server-only\\\"; export { createKokoroClient } from \\\"@/pipeline/kokoro\\\";` if that type-checks and builds; otherwise say so. Test the budget and lock adapters with `createMemoryKV()`.\\n\\n## 6. Contract `docs/contracts/narration.md`\\nDocument: chapter unit and why; the manifest shape and `sceneSpan`; cache key (hash of normalized chapter text + voice + model + speed + format), Blob paths, Redis index and lock (TTL 300 s, dedupes concurrent requests so a second reader gets it free); spend accounting (reserve the estimate on both caps only when generating, refund on failure, cache hits are free, global DAILY_SPEND_CAP_USD applies); the owner's rolling window for uploads (at uploa