ual from `actualNarrationMicro(gpuSec)` summed). Print one line per chapter (`ch 3: generated 412.5 s audio, 7.1 s gpu` or `ch 3: cached`) and a cost summary.\\n- `build.ts`: `--step narrate` creates the Kokoro client lazily only when the step runs; `--dry-run` covers it. Narration needs neither META_API_KEY nor JEV_API_KEY.\\n- Tests for runNarrate with a fake synthesize and a temp dir: writes manifests for every chapter, second run is all cached with zero cost, cap refusal stops spending.\\n\\n## 5. Server cache adapters `server/narration/cache.ts` (no route yet)\\n`import \\\"server-only\\\"`. `createNarrationDeps({ kv, env, synthesize })` returning NarrationDeps for the future upload route: index in Redis under `narr:idx:<key>` (JSON, validated with parseChapterNarration on read), lock `narr:lock:<key>` via `kv.setNxEx(…, token, 300)` and `kv.releaseIfToken`, Blob store as above (server version), budget reserving on BOTH the global spend key and the daily spend key from core/images (`spendKey()`, `dailySpendKey(day)`) against `env.spendCapMicro` / `env.dailySpendCapMicro`, refunding both if either cap is passed (same pattern as server/images/orchestrate.ts). A BYOK path is not part of narration (narration always uses our Modal credits). Plus `server/narration/kokoro.ts` = `import \\\"server-only\\\"; export { createKokoroClient } from \\\"@/pipeline/kokoro\\\";` if that type-checks and builds; otherwise say so. Test the budget and lock adapters with `createMemoryKV()`.\\n\\n## 6. Contract `docs/contracts/narration.md`\\nDocument: chapter unit and why; the manifest shape and `sceneSpan`; cache key (hash of normalized chapter text + voice + model + speed + format), Blob paths, Redis index and lock (TTL 300 s, dedupes concurrent requests so a second reader gets it free); spend accounting (reserve the estimate on both caps only when generating, refund on failure, cache hits are free, global DAILY_SPEND_CAP_USD applies); the owner's rolling window for uploads (at upload chapters 1 and 2 while the book is processed; entering chapter N ensures N+1 and N+2; jumping to N ensures N and N+1; the client asks, the server dedupes); cold start (about 15–30 s for the first chapter after the function scaled to zero, warm calls a few seconds per chapter; the 2-ahead window hides it after chapter 1; while a chapter is pending the Read aloud control shows a quiet \\\"Getting the voice ready…\\\" state); cost per chapter (formula plus a worked number: an average Oz chapter of ~9,000 chars ≈ 10 min of audio ≈ USD 0.003 warm); Oz is pregenerated through the same keys; Modal is deployed with `modal deploy pipeline/modal/narrate.py` and scales to zero, and `modal app stop lectoria-narration` removes it entirely; open items (upload route wiring, Blob vs public/ for Oz). Link it from docs/contracts/book-data.md in one line. Also write docs/tasks/40-narration.md (short design: what and why) and add a BUILT_DURING_HACKATHON.md row in the existing format. Add `NARRATION_CAP_USD` to `.env.example` (name only).\\n\\n## Done when\\n`npm test`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm run check:size`, `npm run check:secrets`, `npm run test:hooks` pass, and `npx tsx pipeline/build.ts oz --step narrate --dry-run` prints `narrate: redo (no previous output)`. `python3 -m py_compile pipeline/modal/narrate.py` passes. Commit in a few focused commits (imperative subjects under 72 chars, bodies say why). Do not push. End with a short summary of files and anything you could not do.\\n\",\"run_stream\":{\"id\":\"01a182fd-1d24-7451-81eb-d015551c1a5a\",\"kind\":\"run\"}}}\nagent-logs/prompts/40-impl.md:17:- Cost: `KOKORO_L4_USD_PER_SEC = 0.000222` (Modal L4, about USD 0.80/h) and `estimateNarrationMicro(chars: number): number` = ceil((chars / 15 * 0.02 + 8) * KOKORO_L4_USD_PER_SEC * 1e6): about 15 chars of audio per second, GPU time about 2% of audio after encode, plus 8 s of cold start/overhead. `actualNarrationMicro(gpuSec)` = ceil(gpuSec * rate * 1e6). Integer micro-dollars, as the repo rules require.\nagent-logs/prompts/40-impl.md:33:  Flow, in this order: key => `index.get` hit => ready cached, cost 0, no lock, no budget. Miss => `store.getManifest` hit => `index.set` backfill, ready cached. Miss => `lock.acquire` (null => pending). Then re-check the index once (another holder may have just finished). Then `budget.reserve(estimateNarrationMicro(totalChars))` (false => release, error budget). Then synthesize (validate `spans.length === texts.length`, else failed), putAudio, build and validate the manifest with `parseChapterNarration`, putManifest, index.set, release, return ready with `cached: false` and `costMicro` = the reserved estimate (the cap counts what was reserved; never refund on success). Any throw after the reserve => refund once, release, error failed. Release failures are swallowed (the lock has a TTL). Never put error text in the result. Spend is counted only when audio is generated, never on hits. Tests with in-memory fakes: hit from index, hit from store with backfill, concurrent second caller gets pending while the first holds the lock, budget refusal releases the lock and never synthesizes, synthesize/store failure refunds exactly once and releases, success counts the estimate, a second call after success is a free hit, and the manifest timings round-trip through `sceneSpan` and `activeChunkAt`.\nagent-logs/40-review-1.jsonl:104:{\"schema_version\":1,\"id\":\"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c41b\",\"stream\":{\"kind\":\"session\",\"id\":\"01a18303-8a86-7fb0-9538-954ee31908b3\"},\"sequence\":104,\"recorded_at\":1780531400000203,\"record_type\":\"event\",\"durability\":\"durable\",\"causation_id\":\"01a18303-8c7e-7df2-afb2-bf2baeb933e8\",\"payload_type\":\"task.lifecycle.output\",\"payload_schema_version\":1,\"payload\":{\"command_id\":\"01a18303-8c7e-7df2-afb2-bf2baeb933e8\",\"event\":{\"chunk\":\"Read text file `core/narration.ts`.\\n1|// Pure narration logic: sentence split, chunking, cache keys, manifest\\n2|// validation, playback helpers, and cost math. No env, no network,\\n3|// no crypto, no node: imports; callers inject hashing.\\n4|export const NARRATION_VOICE = \\\"af_heart\\\";\\n5|export const NARRATION_MODEL = \\\"kokoro-82m/0.9.4\\\";\\n6|export const NARRATION_SPEED = 0.95;\\n7|export const NARRATION_FORMAT = 1;\\n8|export const SENTENCE_GAP_SEC = 0.3;\\n9|export const PARAGRAPH_GAP_SEC = 0.7;\\n10|\\n11|export interface SentenceSpan {\\n12|  start: number;\\n13|  end: number;\\n14|}\\n15|\\n16|export interface NarrationChunk {\\n17|  n: number;\\n18|  start: number;\\n19|  end: number;\\n20|  text: string;\\n21|}\\n22|\\n23|const CLOSERS = new Set([\\\"”\\\", \\\"’\\\", '\\\"', \\\"'\\\", \\\")\\\", \\\"]\\\"]);\\n24|\\n25|// Lowercase words that end with a period without ending a sentence.\\n26|const ABBREVIATIONS = new Set([\\n27|  \\\"mr\\\", \\\"mrs\\\", \\\"ms\\\", \\\"dr\\\", \\\"st\\\", \\\"mt\\\", \\\"prof\\\", \\\"sr\\\", \\\"jr\\\",\\n28|  \\\"rev\\\", \\\"lt\\\", \\\"col\\\", \\\"gen\\\", \\\"capt\\\", \\\"sgt\\\", \\\"ave\\\", \\\"blvd\\\", \\\"rd\\\", \\\"no\\\",\\n29|]);\\n30|\\n31|function isTerminator(char: string): boolean {\\n32|  return char === \\\".\\\" || char === \\\"!\\\" || char === \\\"?\\\" || char === \\\"…\\\";\\n33|}\\n34|\\n35|function isSpace(char: string | undefined): boolean {\\n36|  return char === undefined || /\\\\s/.test(char);\\n37|}\\n38|\\n39|// Word of letters directly before index (exclusive), lowercased.\\n40|function wordBefore(text: string, index: number): string {\\n41|  let i = index - 1;\\n42|  while (i >= 0 && /[A-Za-z]/.test(text[i] as string)) i -= 1;\\n43|  return text.slice(i + 1, index).toLowerCase();\\n44|}\\n45|\\n46|function wordCount(piece: string): number {\\n47|  const words = piece.split(/\\\\s+/).filter((w) => w.length > 0);\\n48|  return words.length;\\n49|}\\n50|\\n51|// Char offsets into the paragraph text, trimmed of surrounding\\n52|// whitespace, covering every non-space char. A sentence ends at a\\n53|// terminator plus closing quotes/brackets followed by whitespace.\\n54|export function splitSentences(text: string): SentenceSpan[] {\\n55|  const raw: SentenceSpan[] = [];\\n56|  let pieceStart = -1;\\n57|  let i = 0;\\n58|  while (i < text.length) {\\n59|    const char = text[i] as string;\\n60|    if (/\\\\s/.test(char)) {\\n61|      i += 1;\\n62|      continue;\\n63|    }\\n64|    if (pieceStart === -1) pieceStart = i;\\n65|    if (isTerminator(char)) {\\n66|      let end = i + 1;\\n67|      while (end < text.length && CLOSERS.has(text[end] as string)) end += 1;\\n68|      if (isSpace(text[end])) {\\n69|        if (char === \\\".\\\") {\\n70|          const word = wordBefore(text, i);\\n71|          const singleInitial = /^[A-Z]$/.test(text.slice(i - 1, i));\\n72|          if (singleInitial || ABBREVIATIONS.has(word)) {\\n73|            i += 1;\\n74|            continue;\\n75|          }\\n76|        }\\n77|        // Trim trailing whitespace inside the piece (there is none:\\n78|        // the piece ends at a terminator or closer).\\n79|        raw.push({ start: pieceStart, end });\\n80|        pieceStart = -1;\\n81|        i = end;\\n82|        continue;\\n83|      }\\n84|    }\\n85|    i += 1;\\n86|  }\\n87|  if (pieceStart !== -1) {\\n88|    let end = text.length;\\n89|    while (end > pieceStart && /\\\\s/.test(text[end - 1] as string)) end -= 1;\\n90|    raw.push({ start: pieceStart, end });\\n91|  }\\n92|  if (raw.length === 0) return [];\\n93|  // Merge a piece shorter than 3 words into the previous sentence\\n94|  // (or the next one if first), keeping offsets exact.\\n95|  const merged: SentenceSpan[] = [];\\n96|  for (const span of raw) {\\n97|    const piece = text.slice(span.start, span.end);\\n98|    if (wordCount(piece) >= 3 || merged.length === 0) {\\n99|      merged.push({ ...span });\\n100|      continue;\\n101|    }\\n102|    const prev = merged[merged.length - 1] as SentenceSpan;\\n103|    prev.end = span.end;\\n104|  }\\n105|  if (merged.length > 1) {\\n106|    const first = merged[0] as SentenceSpan;\\n107|    if (wordCount(text.slice(first.start, first.end)) < 3) {\\n108|      const next = merged[1] as SentenceSpan;\\n109|      next.start = first.start;\\n110|      merged.shift();\\n111|    }\\n112|  }\\n113|  return merged;\\n114|}\\n115|\\n116|export function chapterChunks(paragraphs: { n: number; text: string }[]): {\\n117|  chunks: NarrationChunk[];\\n118|  gaps: number[];\\n119|} {\\n120|  const chunks: NarrationChunk[] = [];\\n121|  const paraOf: number[] = [];\\n122|  paragraphs.forEach((para, paraIndex) => {\\n123|    for (const span of splitSentences(para.text)) {\\n124|      chunks.push({ n: para.n, start: span.start, end: span.end, text: para.text.slice(span.start, span.end) });\\n125|      paraOf.push(paraIndex);\\n126|    }\\n127|  });\\n128|  const gaps = chunks.map((_, i) => {\\n129|    if (i === chunks.length - 1) return 0;\\n130|    return paraOf[i] !== paraOf[i + 1] ? PARAGRAPH_GAP_SEC : SENTENCE_GAP_SEC;\\n131|  });\\n132|  return { chunks, gaps };\\n133|}\\n134|\\n135|export function normalizeChunkText(text: string): string {\\n136|  return text.normalize(\\\"NFC\\\").replace(/\\\\s+/g, \\\" \\\").trim();\\n137|}\\n138|\\n139|// Canonical string the caller hashes with SHA-256. Same text + voice +\\n140|// model + speed => same string; any edit changes it.\\n141|export function narrationKeyInput(args: {\\n142|  chunks: { text: string }[];\\n143|  voice: string;\\n144|  model: string;\\n145|  speed: number;\\n146|  format: number;\\n147|}): string {\\n148|  const body = args.chunks.map((c) => normalizeChunkText(c.text)).join(\\\"\\\\n\\\");\\n149|  return `narration/${args.format}\\\\nvoice:${args.voice}\\\\nmodel:${args.model}\\\\nspeed:${args.speed}\\\\n${body}`;\\n150|}\\n151|\\n152|export function narrationKey(hashHex: string, voice: string): string {\\n153|  return `narration/v${NARRATION_FORMAT}/${voice}/${hashHex.slice(0, 32)}`;\\n154|}\\n155|\\n156|export function narrationAudioPath(key: string): string {\\n157|  return `${key}.mp3`;\\n158|}\\n159|\\n160|export function narrationManifestPath(key: string): string {\\n161|  return `${key}.json`;\\n162|}\\n163|\\n164|export interface ChapterChunkTiming {\\n165|  n: number;\\n166|  start: number;\\n167|  end: number;\\n168|  t0: number;\\n169|  t1: number;\\n170|}\\n171|\\n172|export interface ChapterNarration {\\n173|  format: 1;\\n174|  key: string;\\n175|  src: string;\\n176|  durationSec: number;\\n177|  voice: string;\\n178|  model: string;\\n179|  speed: number;\\n180|  chunks: ChapterChunkTiming[];\\n181|}\\n182|\\n183|function isRecord(json: unknown): json is Record<string, unknown> {\\n184|  return typeof json === \\\"object\\\" && json !== null && !Array.isArray(json);\\n185|}\\n186|\\n187|// Strict parse at the trust boundary: the reader fetches this JSON,\\n188|// so any bad field throws instead of half-playing.\\n189|export function parseChapterNarration(json: unknown): ChapterNarration {\\n190|  if (!isRecord(json)) throw new Error(\\\"invalid narration manifest\\\");\\n191|  if (json.format !== NARRATION_FORMAT) throw new Error(\\\"invalid narration manifest\\\");\\n192|  if (typeof json.key !== \\\"string\\\" || json.key.length === 0) throw new Error(\\\"invalid narration manifest\\\");\\n193|  if (typeof json.src !== \\\"string\\\" || !isSafeSrc(json.src)) throw new Error(\\\"invalid narration manifest\\\");\\n194|  if (typeof json.durationSec !== \\\"number\\\" || !Number.isFinite(json.durationSec) || json.durationSec <= 0) {\\n195|    throw new Error(\\\"invalid narration manifest\\\");\\n196|  }\\n197|  if (typeof json.voice !== \\\"string\\\" || json.voice.length === 0) throw new Error(\\\"invalid narration manifest\\\");\\n198|  if (typeof json.model !== \\\"string\\\" || json.model.length === 0) throw new Error(\\\"invalid narration manifest\\\");\\n199|  if (typeof json.speed !== \\\"number\\\" || !Number.isFinite(json.speed)) throw new Error(\\\"invalid narration manifest\\\");\\n200|  if (!Array.isArray(json.chunks) || json.chunks.length === 0) throw new Error(\\\"invalid narration manifest\\\");\\n201|  const chunks: ChapterChunkTiming[] = json.chunks.map((entry) => {\\n202|    if (!isRecord(entry)) throw new Error(\\\"invalid narration manifest\\\");\\n203|    const { n, start, end, t0, t1 } = entry;\\n204|    if (typeof n !== \\\"number\\\" || !Number.isInteger(n)) throw new Error(\\\"invalid narration manifest\\\");\\n205|    if (typeof start !== \\\"number\\\" || !Number.isInteger(start) || start < 0) throw new Error(\\\"invalid narration manifest\\\");\\n206|    if (typeof end !== \\\"number\\\" || !Number.isInteger(end) || end <= start) throw new Error(\\\"invalid narration manifest\\\");\\n207|    for (const t of [t0, t1]) {\\n208|      if (typeof t !== \\\"number\\\" || !Number.isFinite(t)) throw new Error(\\\"invalid narration manifest\\\");\\n209|    }\\n210|    const from = t0 as number;\\n211|    const to = t1 as number;\\n212|    if (!(0 <= from && from < to && to <= (json.durationSec as number) + 0.05)) {\\n213|      throw new Error(\\\"invalid narration manifest\\\");\\n214|    }\\n215|    return { n: n as number, start: start as number, end: end as number, t0: from, t1: to };\\n216|  });\\n217|  for (let i = 1; i < chunks.length; i++) {\\n218|    if ((chunks[i] as ChapterChunkTiming).t0 < (chunks[i - 1] as ChapterChunkTiming).t0) {\\n219|      throw new Error(\\\"invalid narration manifest\\\");\\n220|    }\\n221|  }\\n222|  return {\\n223|    format: 1,\\n224|    key: json.key as string,\\n225|    src: json.src as string,\\n226|    durationSec: json.durationSec as number,\\n227|    voice: json.voice as string,\\n228|    model: json.model as string,\\n229|    speed: json.speed as number,\\n230|    chunks,\\n231|  };\\n232|}\\n233|\\n234|function isSafeSrc(src: string): boolean {\\n235|  if (src.startsWith(\\\"/narration/\\\")) return true;\\n236|  if (src.startsWith(\\\"https://\\\")) {\\n237|    try {\\n238|      new URL(src);\\n239|      return true;\\n240|    } catch {\\n241|      return false;\\n242|    }\\n243|  }\\n244|  return false;\\n245|}\\n246|\\n247|// Binary search: index of the last chunk with t0 <= t, so the highlight\\n248|// stays on a sentence through the gap after it. -1 before the first.\\n249|export function activeChunkAt(chunks: { t0: number }[], tSec: number): number {\\n250|  let lo = 0;\\n251|  let hi = chunks.length - 1;\\n252|  let found = -1;\\n253|  while (lo <= hi) {\\n254|    const mid = (lo + hi) >> 1;\\n255|    if ((chunks[mid] as { t0: number }).t0 <= tSec) {\\n256|      found = mid;\\n257|      lo = mid + 1;\\n258|    } else {\\n259|      hi = mid - 1;\\n260|    }\\n261|  }\\n262|  return found;\\n263|}\\n264|\\n265|// Playback range for a scene: t0 of the first chunk with n >= startN\\n266|// through t1 of the last chunk with n <= endN. Null when empty.\\n267|export function sceneSpan(\\n268|  narration: { chunks: { n: number; t0: number; t1: number }[] },\\n269|  startN: number,\\n270|  endN: number,\\n271|): { startSec: number; endSec: number } | null {\\n272|  let startSec: number | null = null;\\n273|  let endSec: number | null = null;\\n274|  for (const chunk of narration.chunks) {\\n275|    if (chunk.n < startN || chunk.n > endN) continue;\\n276|    if (startSec === null) startSec = chunk.t0;\\n277|    endSec = chunk.t1;\\n278|  }\\n279|  if (startSec === null || endSec === null) return null;\\n280|  return { startSec, endSec };\\n281|}\\n282|\\n283|export type PrepareEvent = \\\"upload\\\" | \\\"enter\\\" | \\\"jump\\\";\\n284|\\n285|// Owner's rolling window: upload warms chapters 1-2 while the book is\\n286|// processed; entering N warms N+1 and N+2; jumping to N warms N and N+1.\\n287|export function chaptersToPrepare(event: PrepareEvent, ch: number, totalChapters: number): number[] {\\n288|  const wanted = event === \\\"upload\\\" ? [1, 2] : event === \\\"enter\\\" ? [ch + 1, ch + 2] : [ch, ch + 1];\\n289|  const seen = new Set<number>();\\n290|  const out: number[] = [];\\n291|  for (const n of wanted) {\\n292|    if (n < 1 || n > totalChapters || seen.has(n)) continue;\\n293|    seen.add(n);\\n294|    out.push(n);\\n295|  }\\n296|  return out;\\n297|}\\n298|\\n299|// Modal L4, about USD 0.80/h.\\n300|export const KOKORO_L4_USD_PER_SEC = 0.000222;\\n301|\\n302|// About 15 chars of audio per second, GPU time about 2% of audio after\\n303|// encode, plus 8 s of cold start/overhead. Integer micro-dollars.\\n304|export function estimateNarrationMicro(chars: number): number {\\n305|  return Math.ceil((Math.max(0, chars) / 15 * 0.02 + 8) * KOKORO_L4_USD_PER_SEC * 1e6);\\n306|}\\n307|\\n308|export function actualNarrationMicro(gpuSec: number): number {\\n309|  return Math.ceil(Math.max(0, gpuSec) * KOKORO_L4_USD_PER_SEC * 1e6);\\n310|}\",\"final_result\":true,\"kind\":\"output\",\"task_id\":\"01a18303-a324-7730-84d1-f984d3696c12\"},\"kind\":\"task_lifecycle\",\"run_stream\":{\"id\":\"01a18303-8c7e-7df2-afb2-bf2baeb933e8\",\"kind\":\"run\"},\"task_id\":\"01a18303-a324-7730-84d1-f984d3696c12\",\"task_stream\":{\"id\":\"01a18303-a324-7730-84d1-f984d3696c12\",\"kind\":\"task\"}}}\nagent-logs/40-review-1.jsonl:107:{\"schema_version\":1,\"id\":\"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c421\",\"stream\":{\"kind\":\"session\",\"id\":\"01a18303-8a86-7fb0-9538-954ee31908b3\"},\"sequence\":107,\"recorded_at\":1780531400000209,\"record_type\":\"event\",\"durability\":\"durable\",\"causation_id\":\"01a18303-8c7e-7df2-afb2-bf2baeb933e8\",\"payload_type\":\"tool.result\",\"payload_schema_version\":1,\"payload\":{\"call_id\":\"call_01a183039f0674d6b9f42b54b35d84fd\",\"command_id\":\"01a18303-8c7e-7df2-afb2-bf2baeb933e8\",\"correlation_facts\":{\"outcome\":\"success\",\"tool_name\":\"read_file\"},\"kind\":\"tool_result\",\"run_stream\":{\"id\":\"01a18303-8c7e-7df2-afb2-bf2baeb933e8\",\"kind\":\"run\"},\"text\":\"Read text file `core/narration.ts`.\\n1|// Pure narration logic: sentence split, chunking, cache keys, manifest\\n2|// validation, playback helpers, and cost math. No env, no network,\\n3|// no crypto, no node: imports; callers inject hashing.\\n4|export const NARRATION_VOICE = \\\"af_heart\\\";\\n5|export const NARRATION_MODEL = \\\"kokoro-82m/0.9.4\\\";\\n6|export const NARRATION_SPEED = 0.95;\\n7|export const NARRATION_FORMAT = 1;\\n8|export const SENTENCE_GAP_SEC = 0.3;\\n9|export const PARAGRAPH_GAP_SEC = 0.7;\\n10|\\n11|export interface SentenceSpan {\\n12|  start: number;\\n13|  end: number;\\n14|}\\n15|\\n16|export interface NarrationChunk {\\n17|  n: number;\\n18|  start: number;\\n19|  end: number;\\n20|  text: string;\\n21|}\\n22|\\n23|const CLOSERS = new Set([\\\"”\\\", \\\"’\\\", '\\\"', \\\"'\\\", \\\")\\\", \\\"]\\\"]);\\n24|\\n25|// Lowercase words that end with a period without ending a sentence.\\n26|const ABBREVIATIONS = new Set([\\n27|  \\\"mr\\\", \\\"mrs\\\", \\\"ms\\\", \\\"dr\\\", \\\"st\\\", \\\"mt\\\", \\\"prof\\\", \\\"sr\\\", \\\"jr\\\",\\n28|  \\\"rev\\\", \\\"lt\\\", \\\"col\\\", \\\"gen\\\", \\\"capt\\\", \\\"sgt\\\", \\\"ave\\\", \\\"blvd\\\", \\\"rd\\\", \\\"no\\\",\\n29|]);\\n30|\\n31|function isTerminator(char: string): boolean {\\n32|  return char === \\\".\\\" || char === \\\"!\\\" || char === \\\"?\\\" || char === \\\"…\\\";\\n33|}\\n34|\\n35|function isSpace(char: string | undefined): boolean {\\n36|  return char === undefined || /\\\\s/.test(char);\\n37|}\\n38|\\n39|// Word of letters directly before index (exclusive), lowercased.\\n40|function wordBefore(text: string, index: number): string {\\n41|  let i = index - 1;\\n42|  while (i >= 0 && /[A-Za-z]/.test(text[i] as string)) i -= 1;\\n43|  return text.slice(i + 1, index).toLowerCase();\\n44|}\\n45|\\n46|function wordCount(piece: string): number {\\n47|  const words = piece.split(/\\\\s+/).filter((w) => w.length > 0);\\n48|  return words.length;\\n49|}\\n50|\\n51|// Char offsets into the paragraph text, trimmed of surrounding\\n52|// whitespace, covering every non-space char. A sentence ends at a\\n53|// terminator plus closing quotes/brackets followed by whitespace.\\n54|export function splitSentences(text: string): SentenceSpan[] {\\n55|  const raw: SentenceSpan[] = [];\\n56|  let pieceStart = -1;\\n57|  let i = 0;\\n58|  while (i < text.length) {\\n59|    const char = text[i] as string;\\n60|    if (/\\\\s/.test(char)) {\\n61|      i += 1;\\n62|      continue;\\n63|    }\\n64|    if (pieceStart === -1) pieceStart = i;\\n65|    if (isTerminator(char)) {\\n66|      let end = i + 1;\\n67|      while (end < text.length && CLOSERS.has(text[end] as string)) end += 1;\\n68|      if (isSpace(text[end])) {\\n69|        if (char === \\\".\\\") {\\n70|          const word = wordBefore(text, i);\\n71|          const singleInitial = /^[A-Z]$/.test(text.slice(i - 1, i));\\n72|          if (singleInitial || ABBREVIATIONS.has(word)) {\\n73|            i += 1;\\n74|            continue;\\n75|          }\\n76|        }\\n77|        // Trim trailing whitespace inside the piece (there is none:\\n78|        // the piece ends at a terminator or closer).\\n79|        raw.push({ start: pieceStart, end });\\n80|        pieceStart = -1;\\n81|        i = end;\\n82|        continue;\\n83|      }\\n84|    }\\n85|    i += 1;\\n86|  }\\n87|  if (pieceStart !== -1) {\\n88|    let end = text.length;\\n89|    while (end > pieceStart && /\\\\s/.test(text[end - 1] as string)) end -= 1;\\n90|    raw.push({ start: pieceStart, end });\\n91|  }\\n92|  if (raw.length === 0) return [];\\n93|  // Merge a piece shorter than 3 words into the previous sentence\\n94|  // (or the next one if first), keeping offsets exact.\\n95|  const merged: SentenceSpan[] = [];\\n96|  for (const span of raw) {\\n97|    const piece = text.slice(span.start, span.end);\\n98|    if (wordCount(piece) >= 3 || merged.length === 0) {\\n99|      merged.push({ ...span });\\n100|      continue;\\n101|    }\\n102|    const prev = merged[merged.length - 1] as SentenceSpan;\\n103|    prev.end = span.end;\\n104|  }\\n105|  if (merged.length > 1) {\\n106|    const first = merged[0] as SentenceSpan;\\n107|    if (wordCount(text.slice(first.start, first.end)) < 3) {\\n108|      const next = merged[1] as SentenceSpan;\\n109|      next.start = first.start;\\n110|      merged.shift();\\n111|    }\\n112|  }\\n113|  return merged;\\n114|}\\n115|\\n116|export function chapterChunks(paragraphs: { n: number; text: string }[]): {\\n117|  chunks: NarrationChunk[];\\n118|  gaps: number[];\\n119|} {\\n120|  const chunks: NarrationChunk[] = [];\\n121|  const paraOf: number[] = [];\\n122|  paragraphs.forEach((para, paraIndex) => {\\n123|    for (const span of splitSentences(para.text)) {\\n124|      chunks.push({ n: para.n, start: span.start, end: span.end, text: para.text.slice(span.start, span.end) });\\n125|      paraOf.push(paraIndex);\\n126|    }\\n127|  });\\n128|  const gaps = chunks.map((_, i) => {\\n129|    if (i === chunks.length - 1) return 0;\\n130|    return paraOf[i] !== paraOf[i + 1] ? PARAGRAPH_GAP_SEC : SENTENCE_GAP_SEC;\\n131|  });\\n132|  return { chunks, gaps };\\n133|}\\n134|\\n135|export function normalizeChunkText(text: string): string {\\n136|  return text.normalize(\\\"NFC\\\").replace(/\\\\s+/g, \\\" \\\").trim();\\n137|}\\n138|\\n139|// Canonical string the caller hashes with SHA-256. Same text + voice +\\n140|// model + speed => same string; any edit changes it.\\n141|export function narrationKeyInput(args: {\\n142|  chunks: { text: string }[];\\n143|  voice: string;\\n144|  model: string;\\n145|  speed: number;\\n146|  format: number;\\n147|}): string {\\n148|  const body = args.chunks.map((c) => normalizeChunkText(c.text)).join(\\\"\\\\n\\\");\\n149|  return `narration/${args.format}\\\\nvoice:${args.voice}\\\\nmodel:${args.model}\\\\nspeed:${args.speed}\\\\n${body}`;\\n150|}\\n151|\\n152|export function narrationKey(hashHex: string, voice: string): string {\\n153|  return `narration/v${NARRATION_FORMAT}/${voice}/${hashHex.slice(0, 32)}`;\\n154|}\\n155|\\n156|export function narrationAudioPath(key: string): string {\\n157|  return `${key}.mp3`;\\n158|}\\n159|\\n160|export function narrationManifestPath(key: string): string {\\n161|  return `${key}.json`;\\n162|}\\n163|\\n164|export interface ChapterChunkTiming {\\n165|  n: number;\\n166|  start: number;\\n167|  end: number;\\n168|  t0: number;\\n169|  t1: number;\\n170|}\\n171|\\n172|export interface ChapterNarration {\\n173|  format: 1;\\n174|  key: string;\\n175|  src: string;\\n176|  durationSec: number;\\n177|  voice: string;\\n178|  model: string;\\n179|  speed: number;\\n180|  chunks: ChapterChunkTiming[];\\n181|}\\n182|\\n183|function isRecord(json: unknown): json is Record<string, unknown> {\\n184|  return typeof json === \\\"object\\\" && json !== null && !Array.isArray(json);\\n185|}\\n186|\\n187|// Strict parse at the trust boundary: the reader fetches this JSON,\\n188|// so any bad field throws instead of half-playing.\\n189|export function parseChapterNarration(json: unknown): ChapterNarration {\\n190|  if (!isRecord(json)) throw new Error(\\\"invalid narration manifest\\\");\\n191|  if (json.format !== NARRATION_FORMAT) throw new Error(\\\"invalid narration manifest\\\");\\n192|  if (typeof json.key !== \\\"string\\\" || json.key.length === 0) throw new Error(\\\"invalid narration manifest\\\");\\n193|  if (typeof json.src !== \\\"string\\\" || !isSafeSrc(json.src)) throw new Error(\\\"invalid narration manifest\\\");\\n194|  if (typeof json.durationSec !== \\\"number\\\" || !Number.isFinite(json.durationSec) || json.durationSec <= 0) {\\n195|    throw new Error(\\\"invalid narration manifest\\\");\\n196|  }\\n197|  if (typeof json.voice !== \\\"string\\\" || json.voice.length === 0) throw new Error(\\\"invalid narration manifest\\\");\\n198|  if (typeof json.model !== \\\"string\\\" || json.model.length === 0) throw new Error(\\\"invalid narration manifest\\\");\\n199|  if (typeof json.speed !== \\\"number\\\" || !Number.isFinite(json.speed)) throw new Error(\\\"invalid narration manifest\\\");\\n200|  if (!Array.isArray(json.chunks) || json.chunks.length === 0) throw new Error(\\\"invalid narration manifest\\\");\\n201|  const chunks: ChapterChunkTiming[] = json.chunks.map((entry) => {\\n202|    if (!isRecord(entry)) throw new Error(\\\"invalid narration manifest\\\");\\n203|    const { n, start, end, t0, t1 } = entry;\\n204|    if (typeof n !== \\\"number\\\" || !Number.isInteger(n)) throw new Error(\\\"invalid narration manifest\\\");\\n205|    if (typeof start !== \\\"number\\\" || !Number.isInteger(start) || start < 0) throw new Error(\\\"invalid narration manifest\\\");\\n206|    if (typeof end !== \\\"number\\\" || !Number.isInteger(end) || end <= start) throw new Error(\\\"invalid narration manifest\\\");\\n207|    for (const t of [t0, t1]) {\\n208|      if (typeof t !== \\\"number\\\" || !Number.isFinite(t)) throw new Error(\\\"invalid narration manifest\\\");\\n209|    }\\n210|    const from = t0 as number;\\n211|    const to = t1 as number;\\n212|    if (!(0 <= from && from < to && to <= (json.durationSec as number) + 0.05)) {\\n213|      throw new Error(\\\"invalid narration manifest\\\");\\n214|    }\\n215|    return { n: n as number, start: start as number, end: end as number, t0: from, t1: to };\\n216|  });\\n217|  for (let i = 1; i < chunks.length; i++) {\\n218|    if ((chunks[i] as ChapterChunkTiming).t0 < (chunks[i - 1] as ChapterChunkTiming).t0) {\\n219|      throw new Error(\\\"invalid narration manifest\\\");\\n220|    }\\n221|  }\\n222|  return {\\n223|    format: 1,\\n224|    key: json.key as string,\\n225|    src: json.src as string,\\n226|    durationSec: json.durationSec as number,\\n227|    voice: json.voice as string,\\n228|    model: json.model as string,\\n229|    speed: json.speed as number,\\n230|    chunks,\\n231|  };\\n232|}\\n233|\\n234|function isSafeSrc(src: string): boolean {\\n235|  if (src.startsWith(\\\"/narration/\\\")) return true;\\n236|  if (src.startsWith(\\\"https://\\\")) {\\n237|    try {\\n238|      new URL(src);\\n239|      return true;\\n240|    } catch {\\n241|      return false;\\n242|    }\\n243|  }\\n244|  return false;\\n245|}\\n246|\\n247|// Binary search: index of the last chunk with t0 <= t, so the highlight\\n248|// stays on a sentence through the gap after it. -1 before the first.\\n249|export function activeChunkAt(chunks: { t0: number }[], tSec: number): number {\\n250|  let lo = 0;\\n251|  let hi = chunks.length - 1;\\n252|  let found = -1;\\n253|  while (lo <= hi) {\\n254|    const mid = (lo + hi) >> 1;\\n255|    if ((chunks[mid] as { t0: number }).t0 <= tSec) {\\n256|      found = mid;\\n257|      lo = mid + 1;\\n258|    } else {\\n259|      hi = mid - 1;\\n260|    }\\n261|  }\\n262|  return found;\\n263|}\\n264|\\n265|// Playback range for a scene: t0 of the first chunk with n >= startN\\n266|// through t1 of the last chunk with n <= endN. Null when empty.\\n267|export function sceneSpan(\\n268|  narration: { chunks: { n: number; t0: number; t1: number }[] },\\n269|  startN: number,\\n270|  endN: number,\\n271|): { startSec: number; endSec: number } | null {\\n272|  let startSec: number | null = null;\\n273|  let endSec: number | null = null;\\n274|  for (const chunk of narration.chunks) {\\n275|    if (chunk.n < startN || chunk.n > endN) continue;\\n276|    if (startSec === null) startSec = chunk.t0;\\n277|    endSec = chunk.t1;\\n278|  }\\n279|  if (startSec === null || endSec === null) return null;\\n280|  return { startSec, endSec };\\n281|}\\n282|\\n283|export type PrepareEvent = \\\"upload\\\" | \\\"enter\\\" | \\\"jump\\\";\\n284|\\n285|// Owner's rolling window: upload warms chapters 1-2 while the book is\\n286|// processed; entering N warms N+1 and N+2; jumping to N warms N and N+1.\\n287|export function chaptersToPrepare(event: PrepareEvent, ch: number, totalChapters: number): number[] {\\n288|  const wanted = event === \\\"upload\\\" ? [1, 2] : event === \\\"enter\\\" ? [ch + 1, ch + 2] : [ch, ch + 1];\\n289|  const seen = new Set<number>();\\n290|  const out: number[] = [];\\n291|  for (const n of wanted) {\\n292|    if (n < 1 || n > totalChapters || seen.has(n)) continue;\\n293|    seen.add(n);\\n294|    out.push(n);\\n295|  }\\n296|  return out;\\n297|}\\n298|\\n299|// Modal L4, about USD 0.80/h.\\n300|export const KOKORO_L4_USD_PER_SEC = 0.000222;\\n301|\\n302|// About 15 chars of audio per second, GPU time about 2% of audio after\\n303|// encode, plus 8 s of cold start/overhead. Integer micro-dollars.\\n304|export function estimateNarrationMicro(chars: number): number {\\n305|  return Math.ceil((Math.max(0, chars) / 15 * 0.02 + 8) * KOKORO_L4_USD_PER_SEC * 1e6);\\n306|}\\n307|\\n308|export function actualNarrationMicro(gpuSec: number): number {\\n309|  return Math.ceil(Math.max(0, gpuSec) * KOKORO_L4_USD_PER_SEC * 1e6);\\n310|}\"}}\nagent-logs/40-review-1.jsonl:140:{\"schema_version\":1,\"id\":\"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c463\",\"stream\":{\"kind\":\"session\",\"id\":\"01a18303-8a86-7fb0-9538-954ee31908b3\"},\"sequence\":140,\"recorded_at\":1780531400000275,\"record_type\":\"event\",\"durability\":\"durable\",\"causation_id\":\"01a18303-8c7e-7df2-afb2-bf2baeb933e8\",\"payload_type\":\"task.lifecycle.output\",\"payload_schema_version\":1,\"payload\":{\"command_id\":\"01a18303-8c7e-7df2-afb2-bf2baeb933e8\",\"event\":{\"chunk\":\"Read text file `core/narration-cache.ts`.\\n1|// Shared narration cache flow: key -> index -> store -> lock -> budget\\n2|// -> synthesize -> put -> index. Used offline for Oz now and on demand\\n3|// for uploaded books later. Pure: every side effect arrives via deps.\\n4|import {\\n5|  NARRATION_FORMAT,\\n6|  NARRATION_MODEL,\\n7|  NARRATION_SPEED,\\n8|  NARRATION_VOICE,\\n9|  estimateNarrationMicro,\\n10|  narrationKey,\\n11|  narrationKeyInput,\\n12|  parseChapterNarration,\\n13|} from \\\"./narration\\\";\\n14|import type { ChapterNarration, NarrationChunk } from \\\"./narration\\\";\\n15|\\n16|export interface NarrationDeps {\\n17|  sha256Hex(text: string): Promise<string>;\\n18|  index: {\\n19|    get(key: string): Promise<ChapterNarration | null>;\\n20|    set(key: string, value: ChapterNarration): Promise<void>;\\n21|  };\\n22|  store: {\\n23|    getManifest(key: string): Promise<ChapterNarration | null>;\\n24|    putAudio(key: string, mp3: Uint8Array): Promise<string>;\\n25|    putManifest(key: string, value: ChapterNarration): Promise<void>;\\n26|  };\\n27|  lock?: {\\n28|    acquire(key: string): Promise<string | null>;\\n29|    release(key: string, token: string): Promise<void>;\\n30|  };\\n31|  budget?: {\\n32|    reserve(micro: number): Promise<boolean>;\\n33|    refund(micro: number): Promise<void>;\\n34|  };\\n35|  synthesize(req: {\\n36|    texts: string[];\\n37|    gaps: number[];\\n38|    voice: string;\\n39|    speed: number;\\n40|  }): Promise<{\\n41|    mp3: Uint8Array;\\n42|    durationSec: number;\\n43|    spans: { t0: number; t1: number }[];\\n44|    gpuSec: number;\\n45|  }>;\\n46|}\\n47|\\n48|export type EnsureResult =\\n49|  | { status: \\\"ready\\\"; narration: ChapterNarration; cached: boolean; costMicro: number }\\n50|  | { status: \\\"pending\\\" }\\n51|  | { status: \\\"error\\\"; code: \\\"budget\\\" | \\\"failed\\\" };\\n52|\\n53|export async function ensureChapterNarration(\\n54|  input: { chunks: NarrationChunk[]; gaps: number[]; voice?: string; speed?: number },\\n55|  deps: NarrationDeps,\\n56|): Promise<EnsureResult> {\\n57|  const voice = input.voice ?? NARRATION_VOICE;\\n58|  const speed = input.speed ?? NARRATION_SPEED;\\n59|  const hash = await deps.sha256Hex(\\n60|    narrationKeyInput({ chunks: input.chunks, voice, model: NARRATION_MODEL, speed, format: NARRATION_FORMAT }),\\n61|  );\\n62|  const key = narrationKey(hash, voice);\\n63|\\n64|  const indexed = await deps.index.get(key);\\n65|  if (indexed) return { status: \\\"ready\\\", narration: indexed, cached: true, costMicro: 0 };\\n66|\\n67|  const stored = await deps.store.getManifest(key);\\n68|  if (stored) {\\n69|    await deps.index.set(key, stored);\\n70|    return { status: \\\"ready\\\", narration: stored, cached: true, costMicro: 0 };\\n71|  }\\n72|\\n73|  let lease: string | null = null;\\n74|  if (deps.lock) {\\n75|    lease = await deps.lock.acquire(key);\\n76|    if (lease === null) return { status: \\\"pending\\\" };\\n77|    // Another holder may have just finished while we waited.\\n78|    const raced = await deps.index.get(key);\\n79|    if (raced) {\\n80|      await releaseQuietly(deps, key, lease);\\n81|      return { status: \\\"ready\\\", narration: raced, cached: true, costMicro: 0 };\\n82|    }\\n83|  }\\n84|\\n85|  const release = async (): Promise<void> => {\\n86|    if (deps.lock && lease !== null) await releaseQuietly(deps, key, lease);\\n87|  };\\n88|\\n89|  const totalChars = input.chunks.reduce((sum, c) => sum + c.text.length, 0);\\n90|  const estimate = estimateNarrationMicro(totalChars);\\n91|  if (deps.budget) {\\n92|    const ok = await deps.budget.reserve(estimate);\\n93|    if (!ok) {\\n94|      await release();\\n95|      return { status: \\\"error\\\", code: \\\"budget\\\" };\\n96|    }\\n97|  }\\n98|\\n99|  let refunded = false;\\n100|  const refundOnce = async (): Promise<void> => {\\n101|    if (deps.budget && !refunded) {\\n102|      refunded = true;\\n103|      try {\\n104|        await deps.budget.refund(estimate);\\n105|      } catch {\\n106|        // The cap is advisory; a lost refund only skews accounting.\\n107|      }\\n108|    }\\n109|  };\\n110|\\n111|  try {\\n112|    const out = await deps.synthesize({ texts: input.chunks.map((c) => c.text), gaps: input.gaps, voice, speed });\\n113|    if (out.spans.length !== input.chunks.length) throw new Error(\\\"span count mismatch\\\");\\n114|    const src = await deps.store.putAudio(key, out.mp3);\\n115|    const manifest = parseChapterNarration({\\n116|      format: NARRATION_FORMAT,\\n117|      key,\\n118|      src,\\n119|      durationSec: out.durationSec,\\n120|      voice,\\n121|      model: NARRATION_MODEL,\\n122|      speed,\\n123|      chunks: input.chunks.map((chunk, i) => ({\\n124|        n: chunk.n,\\n125|        start: chunk.start,\\n126|        end: chunk.end,\\n127|        t0: (out.spans[i] as { t0: number; t1: number }).t0,\\n128|        t1: (out.spans[i] as { t0: number; t1: number }).t1,\\n129|      })),\\n130|    });\\n131|    await deps.store.putManifest(key, manifest);\\n132|    await deps.index.set(key, manifest);\\n133|    await release();\\n134|    // The cap counts what was reserved; never refund on success.\\n135|    return { status: \\\"ready\\\", narration: manifest, cached: false, costMicro: estimate };\\n136|  } catch {\\n137|    await refundOnce();\\n138|    await release();\\n139|    return { status: \\\"error\\\", code: \\\"failed\\\" };\\n140|  }\\n141|}\\n142|\\n143|async function releaseQuietly(deps: NarrationDeps, key: string, token: string): Promise<void> {\\n144|  try {\\n145|    await deps.lock?.release(key, token);\\n146|  } catch {\\n147|    // The lock has a TTL; a lost release expires on its own.\\n148|  }\\n149|}\",\"final_result\":true,\"kind\":\"output\",\"task_id\":\"01a18303-abf9-7813-81eb-6758509e7995\"},\"kind\":\"task_lifecycle\",\"run_stream\":{\"id\":\"01a18303-8c7e-7df2-afb2-bf2baeb933e8\",\"kind\":\"run\"},\"task_id\":\"01a18303-abf9-7813-81eb-6758509e7995\",\"task_stream\":{\"id\":\"01a18303-abf9-7813-81eb-6758509e7995\",\"kind\":\"task\"}}}\nagent-logs/40-review-1.jsonl:144:{\"schema_version\":1,\"id\":\"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c46b\",\"stream\":{\"kind\":\"session\",\"id\":\"01a18303-8a86-7fb0-9538-954ee31908b3\"},\"sequence\":144,\"recorded_at\":1780531400000283,\"record_type\":\"event\",\"durability\":\"durable\",\"causation_id\":\"01a18303-8c7e-7df2-afb2-bf2baeb933e8\",\"payload_type\":\"task.lifecycle.output\",\"payload_schema_version\":1,\"payload\":{\"command_id\":\"01a18303-8c7e-7df2-afb2-bf2baeb933e8\",\"event\":{\"chunk\":\"Read text file `core/narration.test.ts`.\\n1|import { createHash } from \\\"node:crypto\\\";\\n2|import { describe, expect, it } from \\\"vitest\\\";\\n3|import {\\n4|  NARRATION_FORMAT,\\n5|  NARRATION_MODEL,\\n6|  NARRATION_SPEED,\\n7|  NARRATION_VOICE,\\n8|  PARAGRAPH_GAP_SEC,\\n9|  SENTENCE_GAP_SEC,\\n10|  activeChunkAt,\\n11|  actualNarrationMicro,\\n12|  chapterChunks,\\n13|  chaptersToPrepare,\\n14|  estimateNarrationMicro,\\n15|  narrationKey,\\n16|  narrationKeyInput,\\n17|  parseChapterNarration,\\n18|  sceneSpan,\\n19|  splitSentences,\\n20|} from \\\"./narration\\\";\\n21|\\n22|const OZ = `“I am Oz, the Great and Terrible,” said the little man, in a trembling voice. “But don't strike me — please don't — and I will do anything you want me to do.” “Oh, you're a humbug!” said Dorothy. Mr. H. M. Wogglebug rushed — very fast — toward the door!” said Dorothy, turning pale.`;\\n23|\\n24|// Oz-style text: curly quotes, a dialogue tag after a quoted sentence,\\n25|// and a quote ending the paragraph (see OZ for em dashes and Mr.).\\n26|const OZ_PARA = \\\"\\\\u201cYou have plenty of courage, I am sure,\\\\u201d answered Oz. \\\\u201cAll you need is confidence in yourself.\\\\u201d\\\\n\\\"\\n27|\\n28|describe(\\\"splitSentences\\\", () => {\\n29|  it(\\\"covers every non-space char with trimmed offsets\\\", () => {\\n30|    const spans = splitSentences(OZ_PARA);\\n31|    expect(spans.length).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n32|    for (const span of spans) {\\n33|      expect(OZ_PARA[span.start]).toMatch(/\\\\S/);\\n34|      expect(OZ_PARA[span.end - 1]).toMatch(/\\\\S/);\\n35|    }\\n36|    const covered = spans.map((s) => OZ_PARA.slice(s.start, s.end).replace(/\\\\s+/g, \\\" \\\").trim()).join(\\\" \\\");\\n37|    expect(covered.replace(/\\\\s+/g, \\\" \\\").trim()).toBe(OZ_PARA.replace(/\\\\s+/g, \\\" \\\").trim());\\n38|  });\\n39|\\n40|  it(\\\"does not end after Mr. or a single capital initial\\\", () => {\\n41|    const spans = splitSentences(`Mr. H. M. Wogglebug rushed toward the door and knocked loudly.`);\\n42|    expect(spans).toHaveLength(1);\\n43|  });\\n44|\\n45|  it(\\\"ends at ! and ? plus closing quotes before whitespace\\\", () => {\\n46|    const spans = splitSentences(`“Oh, you're a humbug!” said Dorothy. Are you quite sure about that?`);\\n47|    expect(spans).toHaveLength(2);\\n48|    // \\\"said Dorothy.\\\" is two words, so it merges into the sentence before it.\\n49|    expect(spans[0]).toEqual({ start: 0, end: `“Oh, you're a humbug!” said Dorothy.`.length });\\n50|  });\\n51|\\n52|  it(\\\"ends a paragraph-final quote without trailing space\\\", () => {\\n53|    const text = `She whispered, “do not be afraid.”`;\\n54|    const spans = splitSentences(text);\\n55|    expect(spans).toHaveLength(1);\\n56|    expect(spans[0]).toEqual({ start: 0, end: text.length });\\n57|  });\\n58|\\n59|  it(\\\"merges a sub-3-word piece into its neighbor\\\", () => {\\n60|    const spans = splitSentences(`The lion roared with tremendous courage. Yes! He ran away quickly.`);\\n61|    const texts = spans.map((s) => `The lion roared with tremendous courage. Yes! He ran away quickly.`.slice(s.start, s.end));\\n62|    expect(texts.some((t) => t === \\\"Yes!\\\")).toBe(false);\\n63|    expect(spans).toHaveLength(2);\\n64|  });\\n65|\\n66|  it(\\\"handles the Oz sample end to end\\\", () => {\\n67|    const spans = splitSentences(OZ);\\n68|    expect(spans.length).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(3);\\n69|    expect(OZ.slice(spans[0]?.start, spans[0]?.end)).toContain(\\\"Great and Terrible\\\");\\n70|  });\\n71|});\\n72|\\n73|describe(\\\"chapterChunks\\\", () => {\\n74|  it(\\\"uses paragraph gaps across paragraphs and sentence gaps within\\\", () => {\\n75|    const { chunks, gaps } = chapterChunks([\\n76|      { n: 1, text: `The road was long and dusty. Dorothy walked on bravely.` },\\n77|      { n: 2, text: `Toto barked at the strange green light ahead.` },\\n78|    ]);\\n79|    expect(chunks).toHaveLength(3);\\n80|    expect(chunks.map((c) => c.n)).toEqual([1, 1, 2]);\\n81|    expect(gaps).toEqual([SENTENCE_GAP_SEC, PARAGRAPH_GAP_SEC, 0]);\\n82|    expect(chunks[0]).toMatchObject({ n: 1, start: 0, text: `The road was long and dusty.` });\\n83|  });\\n84|});\\n85|\\n86|describe(\\\"cache keys\\\", () => {\\n87|  const chunks = [{ text: `  The road was long.\\\\n\\\\nDorothy walked on.` }];\\n88|\\n89|  function hashOf(input: string): string {\\n90|    return createHash(\\\"sha256\\\").update(input).digest(\\\"hex\\\");\\n91|  }\\n92|\\n93|  it(\\\"is stable for the same text and moves on any edit\\\", () => {\\n94|    const base = narrationKeyInput({ chunks, voice: NARRATION_VOICE, model: NARRATION_MODEL, speed: NARRATION_SPEED, format: NARRATION_FORMAT });\\n95|    const same = narrationKeyInput({ chunks: [{ text: \\\"The road was long. Dorothy walked on.\\\" }], voice: NARRATION_VOICE, model: NARRATION_MODEL, speed: NARRATION_SPEED, format: NARRATION_FORMAT });\\n96|    expect(same).toBe(base);\\n97|    const edited = narrationKeyInput({ chunks: [{ text: \\\"The road was long! Dorothy walked on.\\\" }], voice: NARRATION_VOICE, model: NARRATION_MODEL, speed: NARRATION_SPEED, format: NARRATION_FORMAT });\\n98|    expect(edited).not.toBe(base);\\n99|    expect(narrationKeyInput({ chunks, voice: \\\"af_bella\\\", model: NARRATION_MODEL, speed: NARRATION_SPEED, format: NARRATION_FORMAT })).not.toBe(base);\\n100|    expect(narrationKey(hashOf(base), NARRATION_VOICE)).toBe(\\n101|      `narration/v${NARRATION_FORMAT}/${NARRATION_VOICE}/${hashOf(base).slice(0, 32)}`,\\n102|    );\\n103|  });\\n104|});\\n105|\\n106|describe(\\\"parseChapterNarration\\\", () => {\\n107|  const good = {\\n108|    format: 1,\\n109|    key: \\\"narration/v1/af_heart/abc\\\",\\n110|    src: \\\"/narration/v1/af_heart/abc.mp3\\\",\\n111|    durationSec: 10,\\n112|    voice: \\\"af_heart\\\",\\n113|    model: \\\"kokoro-82m/0.9.4\\\",\\n114|    speed: 0.95,\\n115|    chunks: [\\n116|      { n: 1, start: 0, end: 5, t0: 0, t1: 4 },\\n117|      { n: 2, start: 0, end: 7, t0: 4.3, t1: 9.5 },\\n118|    ],\\n119|  };\\n120|\\n121|  it(\\\"accepts a good manifest, including an https src\\\", () => {\\n122|    expect(parseChapterNarration(good).chunks).toHaveLength(2);\\n123|    expect(parseChapterNarration({ ...good, src: \\\"https://cdn.example.com/n.mp3\\\" }).src).toContain(\\\"https://\\\");\\n124|  });\\n125|\\n126|  it(\\\"throws on any bad field\\\", () => {\\n127|    const bad: unknown[] = [\\n128|      null,\\n129|      { ...good, format: 2 },\\n130|      { ...good, src: \\\"http://evil.example.com/n.mp3\\\" },\\n131|      { ...good, src: \\\"/audio/n.mp3\\\" },\\n132|      { ...good, src: \\\"javascript:alert(1)\\\" },\\n133|      { ...good, durationSec: Number.NaN },\\n134|      { ...good, chunks: [] },\\n135|      { ...good, chunks: [{ n: 1.5, start: 0, end: 5, t0: 0, t1: 4 }] },\\n136|      { ...good, chunks: [{ n: 1, start: 5, end: 5, t0: 0, t1: 4 }] },\\n137|      { ...good, chunks: [{ n: 1, start: 0, end: 5, t0: 4, t1: 4 }] },\\n138|      { ...good, chunks: [{ n: 1, start: 0, end: 5, t0: -1, t1: 4 }] },\\n139|      { ...good, chunks: [{ n: 1, start: 0, end: 5, t0: 0, t1: 11 }] },\\n140|      {\\n141|        ...good,\\n142|        chunks: [\\n143|          { n: 1, start: 0, end: 5, t0: 4, t1: 6 },\\n144|          { n: 2, start: 0, end: 5, t0: 0, t1: 3 },\\n145|        ],\\n146|      },\\n147|    ];\\n148|    for (const entry of bad) expect(() => parseChapterNarration(entry)).toThrow();\\n149|  });\\n150|});\\n151|\\n152|describe(\\\"activeChunkAt\\\", () => {\\n153|  const chunks = [{ t0: 0 }, { t0: 4.3 }, { t0: 8 }];\\n154|  it(\\\"holds the highlight through the gap after a sentence\\\", () => {\\n155|    expect(activeChunkAt(chunks, -0.1)).toBe(-1);\\n156|    expect(activeChunkAt(chunks, 0)).toBe(0);\\n157|    expect(activeChunkAt(chunks, 4.2)).toBe(0);\\n158|    expect(activeChunkAt(chunks, 4.3)).toBe(1);\\n159|    expect(activeChunkAt(chunks, 99)).toBe(2);\\n160|  });\\n161|});\\n162|\\n163|describe(\\\"sceneSpan\\\", () => {\\n164|  const narration = {\\n165|    chunks: [\\n166|      { n: 1, t0: 0, t1: 4 },\\n167|      { n: 2, t0: 4.3, t1: 8 },\\n168|      { n: 5, t0: 8.3, t1: 12 },\\n169|    ],\\n170|  };\\n171|  it(\\\"spans the first to the last chunk in range\\\", () => {\\n172|    expect(sceneSpan(narration, 1, 2)).toEqual({ startSec: 0, endSec: 8 });\\n173|    expect(sceneSpan(narration, 2, 4)).toEqual({ startSec: 4.3, endSec: 8 });\\n174|    expect(sceneSpan(narration, 3, 4)).toBeNull();\\n175|  });\\n176|});\\n177|\\n178|describe(\\\"chaptersToPrepare\\\", () => {\\n179|  it(\\\"follows the owner's rolling window\\\", () => {\\n180|    expect(chaptersToPrepare(\\\"upload\\\", 1, 24)).toEqual([1, 2]);\\n181|    expect(chaptersToPrepare(\\\"enter\\\", 5, 24)).toEqual([6, 7]);\\n182|    expect(chaptersToPrepare(\\\"jump\\\", 5, 24)).toEqual([5, 6]);\\n183|    expect(chaptersToPrepare(\\\"enter\\\", 24, 24)).toEqual([]);\\n184|    expect(chaptersToPrepare(\\\"jump\\\", 24, 24)).toEqual([24]);\\n185|    expect(chaptersToPrepare(\\\"upload\\\", 1, 1)).toEqual([1]);\\n186|  });\\n187|});\\n188|\\n189|describe(\\\"cost\\\", () => {\\n190|  it(\\\"estimates an average Oz chapter near USD 0.003 warm\\\", () => {\\n191|    // ~9,000 chars ≈ 10 min of audio: 9000/15*0.02+8 = 20 s GPU.\\n192|    const micro = estimateNarrationMicro(9000);\\n193|    expect(micro).toBe(Math.ceil(20 * 0.000222 * 1e6));\\n194|    expect(micro / 1e6).toBeCloseTo(0.0044, 3);\\n195|    expect(actualNarrationMicro(7.1)).toBe(Math.ceil(7.1 * 0.000222 * 1e6));\\n196|    expect(Number.isInteger(estimateNarrationMicro(0))).toBe(true);\\n197|  });\\n198|});\",\"final_result\":true,\"kind\":\"output\",\"task_id\":\"01a18303-ac07-73c1-ba78-3e6cac37aad1\"},\"kind\":\"task_lifecycle\",\"run_stream\":{\"id\":\"01a18303-8c7e-7df2-afb2-bf2baeb933e8\",\"kind\":\"run\"},\"task_id\":\"01a18303-ac07-73c1-ba78-3e6cac37aad1\",\"task_stream\":{\"id\":\"01a18303-ac07-73c1-ba78-3e6cac37aad1\",\"kind\":\"task\"}}}\nagent-logs/40-review-1.jsonl:146:{\"schema_version\":1,\"id\":\"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c46f\",\"stream\":{\"kind\":\"session\",\"id\":\"01a18303-8a86-7fb0-9538-954ee31908b3\"},\"sequence\":146,\"recorded_at\":1780531400000287,\"record_type\":\"event\",\"durability\":\"durable\",\"causation_id\":\"01a18303-8c7e-7df2-afb2-bf2baeb933e8\",\"payload_type\":\"tool.result\",\"payload_schema_version\":1,\"payload\":{\"call_id\":\"call_01a18303a7f975c6942e672a2c275997\",\"command_id\":\"01a18303-8c7e-7df2-afb2-bf2baeb933e8\",\"correlation_facts\":{\"outcome\":\"success\",\"tool_name\":\"read_file\"},\"kind\":\"tool_result\",\"run_stream\":{\"id\":\"01a18303-8c7e-7df2-afb2-bf2baeb933e8\",\"kind\":\"run\"},\"text\":\"Read text file `core/narration-cache.ts`.\\n1|// Shared narration cache flow: key -> index -> store -> lock -> budget\\n2|// -> synthesize -> put -> index. Used offline for Oz now and on demand\\n3|// for uploaded books later. Pure: every side effect arrives via deps.\\n4|import {\\n5|  NARRATION_FORMAT,\\n6|  NARRATION_MODEL,\\n7|  NARRATION_SPEED,\\n8|  NARRATION_VOICE,\\n9|  estimateNarrationMicro,\\n10|  narrationKey,\\n11|  narrationKeyInput,\\n12|  parseChapterNarration,\\n13|} from \\\"./narration\\\";\\n14|import type { ChapterNarration, NarrationChunk } from \\\"./narration\\\";\\n15|\\n16|export interface NarrationDeps {\\n17|  sha256Hex(text: string): Promise<string>;\\n18|  index: {\\n19|    get(key: string): Promise<ChapterNarration | null>;\\n20|    set(key: string, value: ChapterNarration): Promise<void>;\\n21|  };\\n22|  store: {\\n23|    getManifest(key: string): Promise<ChapterNarration | null>;\\n24|    putAudio(key: string, mp3: Uint8Array): Promise<string>;\\n25|    putManifest(key: string, value: ChapterNarration): Promise<void>;\\n26|  };\\n27|  lock?: {\\n28|    acquire(key: string): Promise<string | null>;\\n29|    release(key: string, token: string): Promise<void>;\\n30|  };\\n31|  budget?: {\\n32|    reserve(micro: number): Promise<boolean>;\\n33|    refund(micro: number): Promise<void>;\\n34|  };\\n35|  synthesize(req: {\\n36|    texts: string[];\\n37|    gaps: number[];\\n38|    voice: string;\\n39|    speed: number;\\n40|  }): Promise<{\\n41|    mp3: Uint8Array;\\n42|    durationSec: number;\\n43|    spans: { t0: number; t1: number }[];\\n44|    gpuSec: number;\\n45|  }>;\\n46|}\\n47|\\n48|export type EnsureResult =\\n49|  | { status: \\\"ready\\\"; narration: ChapterNarration; cached: boolean; costMicro: number }\\n50|  | { status: \\\"pending\\\" }\\n51|  | { status: \\\"error\\\"; code: \\\"budget\\\" | \\\"failed\\\" };\\n52|\\n53|export async function ensureChapterNarration(\\n54|  input: { chunks: NarrationChunk[]; gaps: number[]; voice?: string; speed?: number },\\n55|  deps: NarrationDeps,\\n56|): Promise<EnsureResult> {\\n57|  const voice = input.voice ?? NARRATION_VOICE;\\n58|  const speed = input.speed ?? NARRATION_SPEED;\\n59|  const hash = await deps.sha256Hex(\\n60|    narrationKeyInput({ chunks: input.chunks, voice, model: NARRATION_MODEL, speed, format: NARRATION_FORMAT }),\\n61|  );\\n62|  const key = narrationKey(hash, voice);\\n63|\\n64|  const indexed = await deps.index.get(key);\\n65|  if (indexed) return { status: \\\"ready\\\", narration: indexed, cached: true, costMicro: 0 };\\n66|\\n67|  const stored = await deps.store.getManifest(key);\\n68|  if (stored) {\\n69|    await deps.index.set(key, stored);\\n70|    return { status: \\\"ready\\\", narration: stored, cached: true, costMicro: 0 };\\n71|  }\\n72|\\n73|  let lease: string | null = null;\\n74|  if (deps.lock) {\\n75|    lease = await deps.lock.acquire(key);\\n76|    if (lease === null) return { status: \\\"pending\\\" };\\n77|    // Another holder may have just finished while we waited.\\n78|    const raced = await deps.index.get(key);\\n79|    if (raced) {\\n80|      await releaseQuietly(deps, key, lease);\\n81|      return { status: \\\"ready\\\", narration: raced, cached: true, costMicro: 0 };\\n82|    }\\n83|  }\\n84|\\n85|  const release = async (): Promise<void> => {\\n86|    if (deps.lock && lease !== null) await releaseQuietly(deps, key, lease);\\n87|  };\\n88|\\n89|  const totalChars = input.chunks.reduce((sum, c) => sum + c.text.length, 0);\\n90|  const estimate = estimateNarrationMicro(totalChars);\\n91|  if (deps.budget) {\\n92|    const ok = await deps.budget.reserve(estimate);\\n93|    if (!ok) {\\n94|      await release();\\n95|      return { status: \\\"error\\\", code: \\\"budget\\\" };\\n96|    }\\n97|  }\\n98|\\n99|  let refunded = false;\\n100|  const refundOnce = async (): Promise<void> => {\\n101|    if (deps.budget && !refunded) {\\n102|      refunded = true;\\n103|      try {\\n104|        await deps.budget.refund(estimate);\\n105|      } catch {\\n106|        // The cap is advisory; a lost refund only skews accounting.\\n107|      }\\n108|    }\\n109|  };\\n110|\\n111|  try {\\n112|    const out = await deps.synthesize({ texts: input.chunks.map((c) => c.text), gaps: input.gaps, voice, speed });\\n113|    if (out.spans.length !== input.chunks.length) throw new Error(\\\"span count mismatch\\\");\\n114|    const src = await deps.store.putAudio(key, out.mp3);\\n115|    const manifest = parseChapterNarration({\\n116|      format: NARRATION_FORMAT,\\n117|      key,\\n118|      src,\\n119|      durationSec: out.durationSec,\\n120|      voice,\\n121|      model: NARRATION_MODEL,\\n122|      speed,\\n123|      chunks: input.chunks.map((chunk, i) => ({\\n124|        n: chunk.n,\\n125|        start: chunk.start,\\n126|        end: chunk.end,\\n127|        t0: (out.spans[i] as { t0: number; t1: number }).t0,\\n128|        t1: (out.spans[i] as { t0: number; t1: number }).t1,\\n129|      })),\\n130|    });\\n131|    await deps.store.putManifest(key, manifest);\\n132|    await deps.index.set(key, manifest);\\n133|    await release();\\n134|    // The cap counts what was reserved; never refund on success.\\n135|    return { status: \\\"ready\\\", narration: manifest, cached: false, costMicro: estimate };\\n136|  } catch {\\n137|    await refundOnce();\\n138|    await release();\\n139|    return { status: \\\"error\\\", code: \\\"failed\\\" };\\n140|  }\\n141|}\\n142|\\n143|async function releaseQuietly(deps: NarrationDeps, key: string, token: string): Promise<void> {\\n144|  try {\\n145|    await deps.lock?.release(key, token);\\n146|  } catch {\\n147|    // The lock has a TTL; a lost release expires on its own.\\n148|  }\\n149|}\"}}\nagent-logs/40-review-1.jsonl:148:{\"schema_version\":1,\"id\":\"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c473\",\"stream\":{\"kind\":\"session\",\"id\":\"01a18303-8a86-7fb0-9538-954ee31908b3\"},\"sequence\":148,\"recorded_at\":1780531400000291,\"record_type\":\"event\",\"durability\":\"durable\",\"causation_id\":\"01a18303-8c7e-7df2-afb2-bf2baeb933e8\",\"payload_type\":\"tool.result\",\"payload_schema_version\":1,\"payload\":{\"call_id\":\"call_01a18303aa1670ca86979165b5018524\",\"command_id\":\"01a18303-8c7e-7df2-afb2-bf2baeb933e8\",\"correlation_facts\":{\"outcome\":\"success\",\"tool_name\":\"read_file\"},\"kind\":\"tool_result\",\"run_stream\":{\"id\":\"01a18303-8c7e-7df2-afb2-bf2baeb933e8\",\"kind\":\"run\"},\"text\":\"Read text file `core/narration.test.ts`.\\n1|import { createHash } from \\\"node:crypto\\\";\\n2|import { describe, expect, it } from \\\"vitest\\\";\\n3|import {\\n4|  NARRATION_FORMAT,\\n5|  NARRATION_MODEL,\\n6|  NARRATION_SPEED,\\n7|  NARRATION_VOICE,\\n8|  PARAGRAPH_GAP_SEC,\\n9|  SENTENCE_GAP_SEC,\\n10|  activeChunkAt,\\n11|  actualNarrationMicro,\\n12|  chapterChunks,\\n13|  chaptersToPrepare,\\n14|  estimateNarrationMicro,\\n15|  narrationKey,\\n16|  narrationKeyInput,\\n17|  parseChapterNarration,\\n18|  sceneSpan,\\n19|  splitSentences,\\n20|} from \\\"./narration\\\";\\n21|\\n22|const OZ = `“I am Oz, the Great and Terrible,” said the little man, in a trembling voice. “But don't strike me — please don't — and I will do anything you want me to do.” “Oh, you're a humbug!” said Dorothy. Mr. H. M. Wogglebug rushed — very fast — toward the door!” said Dorothy, turning pale.`;\\n23|\\n24|// Oz-style text: curly quotes, a dialogue tag after a quoted sentence,\\n25|// and a quote ending the paragraph (see OZ for em dashes and Mr.).\\n26|const OZ_PARA = \\\"\\\\u201cYou have plenty of courage, I am sure,\\\\u201d answered Oz. \\\\u201cAll you need is confidence in yourself.\\\\u201d\\\\n\\\"\\n27|\\n28|describe(\\\"splitSentences\\\", () => {\\n29|  it(\\\"covers every non-space char with trimmed offsets\\\", () => {\\n30|    const spans = splitSentences(OZ_PARA);\\n31|    expect(spans.length).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n32|    for (const span of spans) {\\n33|      expect(OZ_PARA[span.start]).toMatch(/\\\\S/);\\n34|      expect(OZ_PARA[span.end - 1]).toMatch(/\\\\S/);\\n35|    }\\n36|    const covered = spans.map((s) => OZ_PARA.slice(s.start, s.end).replace(/\\\\s+/g, \\\" \\\").trim()).join(\\\" \\\");\\n37|    expect(covered.replace(/\\\\s+/g, \\\" \\\").trim()).toBe(OZ_PARA.replace(/\\\\s+/g, \\\" \\\").trim());\\n38|  });\\n39|\\n40|  it(\\\"does not end after Mr. or a single capital initial\\\", () => {\\n41|    const spans = splitSentences(`Mr. H. M. Wogglebug rushed toward the door and knocked loudly.`);\\n42|    expect(spans).toHaveLength(1);\\n43|  });\\n44|\\n45|  it(\\\"ends at ! and ? plus closing quotes before whitespace\\\", () => {\\n46|    const spans = splitSentences(`“Oh, you're a humbug!” said Dorothy. Are you quite sure about that?`);\\n47|    expect(spans).toHaveLength(2);\\n48|    // \\\"said Dorothy.\\\" is two words, so it merges into the sentence before it.\\n49|    expect(spans[0]).toEqual({ start: 0, end: `“Oh, you're a humbug!” said Dorothy.`.length });\\n50|  });\\n51|\\n52|  it(\\\"ends a paragraph-final quote without trailing space\\\", () => {\\n53|    const text = `She whispered, “do not be afraid.”`;\\n54|    const spans = splitSentences(text);\\n55|    expect(spans).toHaveLength(1);\\n56|    expect(spans[0]).toEqual({ start: 0, end: text.length });\\n57|  });\\n58|\\n59|  it(\\\"merges a sub-3-word piece into its neighbor\\\", () => {\\n60|    const spans = splitSentences(`The lion roared with tremendous courage. Yes! He ran away quickly.`);\\n61|    const texts = spans.map((s) => `The lion roared with tremendous courage. Yes! He ran away quickly.`.slice(s.start, s.end));\\n62|    expect(texts.some((t) => t === \\\"Yes!\\\")).toBe(false);\\n63|    expect(spans).toHaveLength(2);\\n64|  });\\n65|\\n66|  it(\\\"handles the Oz sample end to end\\\", () => {\\n67|    const spans = splitSentences(OZ);\\n68|    expect(spans.length).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(3);\\n69|    expect(OZ.slice(spans[0]?.start, spans[0]?.end)).toContain(\\\"Great and Terrible\\\");\\n70|  });\\n71|});\\n72|\\n73|describe(\\\"chapterChunks\\\", () => {\\n74|  it(\\\"uses paragraph gaps across paragraphs and sentence gaps within\\\", () => {\\n75|    const { chunks, gaps } = chapterChunks([\\n76|      { n: 1, text: `The road was long and dusty. Dorothy walked on bravely.` },\\n77|      { n: 2, text: `Toto barked at the strange green light ahead.` },\\n78|    ]);\\n79|    expect(chunks).toHaveLength(3);\\n80|    expect(chunks.map((c) => c.n)).toEqual([1, 1, 2]);\\n81|    expect(gaps).toEqual([SENTENCE_GAP_SEC, PARAGRAPH_GAP_SEC, 0]);\\n82|    expect(chunks[0]).toMatchObject({ n: 1, start: 0, text: `The road was long and dusty.` });\\n83|  });\\n84|});\\n85|\\n86|describe(\\\"cache keys\\\", () => {\\n87|  const chunks = [{ text: `  The road was long.\\\\n\\\\nDorothy walked on.` }];\\n88|\\n89|  function hashOf(input: string): string {\\n90|    return createHash(\\\"sha256\\\").update(input).digest(\\\"hex\\\");\\n91|  }\\n92|\\n93|  it(\\\"is stable for the same text and moves on any edit\\\", () => {\\n94|    const base = narrationKeyInput({ chunks, voice: NARRATION_VOICE, model: NARRATION_MODEL, speed: NARRATION_SPEED, format: NARRATION_FORMAT });\\n95|    const same = narrationKeyInput({ chunks: [{ text: \\\"The road was long. Dorothy walked on.\\\" }], voice: NARRATION_VOICE, model: NARRATION_MODEL, speed: NARRATION_SPEED, format: NARRATION_FORMAT });\\n96|    expect(same).toBe(base);\\n97|    const edited = narrationKeyInput({ chunks: [{ text: \\\"The road was long! Dorothy walked on.\\\" }], voice: NARRATION_VOICE, model: NARRATION_MODEL, speed: NARRATION_SPEED, format: NARRATION_FORMAT });\\n98|    expect(edited).not.toBe(base);\\n99|    expect(narrationKeyInput({ chunks, voice: \\\"af_bella\\\", model: NARRATION_MODEL, speed: NARRATION_SPEED, format: NARRATION_FORMAT })).not.toBe(base);\\n100|    expect(narrationKey(hashOf(base), NARRATION_VOICE)).toBe(\\n101|      `narration/v${NARRATION_FORMAT}/${NARRATION_VOICE}/${hashOf(base).slice(0, 32)}`,\\n102|    );\\n103|  });\\n104|});\\n105|\\n106|describe(\\\"parseChapterNarration\\\", () => {\\n107|  const good = {\\n108|    format: 1,\\n109|    key: \\\"narration/v1/af_heart/abc\\\",\\n110|    src: \\\"/narration/v1/af_heart/abc.mp3\\\",\\n111|    durationSec: 10,\\n112|    voice: \\\"af_heart\\\",\\n113|    model: \\\"kokoro-82m/0.9.4\\\",\\n114|    speed: 0.95,\\n115|    chunks: [\\n116|      { n: 1, start: 0, end: 5, t0: 0, t1: 4 },\\n117|      { n: 2, start: 0, end: 7, t0: 4.3, t1: 9.5 },\\n118|    ],\\n119|  };\\n120|\\n121|  it(\\\"accepts a good manifest, including an https src\\\", () => {\\n122|    expect(parseChapterNarration(good).chunks).toHaveLength(2);\\n123|    expect(parseChapterNarration({ ...good, src: \\\"https://cdn.example.com/n.mp3\\\" }).src).toContain(\\\"https://\\\");\\n124|  });\\n125|\\n126|  it(\\\"throws on any bad field\\\", () => {\\n127|    const bad: unknown[] = [\\n128|      null,\\n129|      { ...good, format: 2 },\\n130|      { ...good, src: \\\"http://evil.example.com/n.mp3\\\" },\\n131|      { ...good, src: \\\"/audio/n.mp3\\\" },\\n132|      { ...good, src: \\\"javascript:alert(1)\\\" },\\n133|      { ...good, durationSec: Number.NaN },\\n134|      { ...good, chunks: [] },\\n135|      { ...good, chunks: [{ n: 1.5, start: 0, end: 5, t0: 0, t1: 4 }] },\\n136|      { ...good, chunks: [{ n: 1, start: 5, end: 5, t0: 0, t1: 4 }] },\\n137|      { ...good, chunks: [{ n: 1, start: 0, end: 5, t0: 4, t1: 4 }] },\\n138|      { ...good, chunks: [{ n: 1, start: 0, end: 5, t0: -1, t1: 4 }] },\\n139|      { ...good, chunks: [{ n: 1, start: 0, end: 5, t0: 0, t1: 11 }] },\\n140|      {\\n141|        ...good,\\n142|        chunks: [\\n143|          { n: 1, start: 0, end: 5, t0: 4, t1: 6 },\\n144|          { n: 2, start: 0, end: 5, t0: 0, t1: 3 },\\n145|        ],\\n146|      },\\n147|    ];\\n148|    for (const entry of bad) expect(() => parseChapterNarration(entry)).toThrow();\\n149|  });\\n150|});\\n151|\\n152|describe(\\\"activeChunkAt\\\", () => {\\n153|  const chunks = [{ t0: 0 }, { t0: 4.3 }, { t0: 8 }];\\n154|  it(\\\"holds the highlight through the gap after a sentence\\\", () => {\\n155|    expect(activeChunkAt(chunks, -0.1)).toBe(-1);\\n156|    expect(activeChunkAt(chunks, 0)).toBe(0);\\n157|    expect(activeChunkAt(chunks, 4.2)).toBe(0);\\n158|    expect(activeChunkAt(chunks, 4.3)).toBe(1);\\n159|    expect(activeChunkAt(chunks, 99)).toBe(2);\\n160|  });\\n161|});\\n162|\\n163|describe(\\\"sceneSpan\\\", () => {\\n164|  const narration = {\\n165|    chunks: [\\n166|      { n: 1, t0: 0, t1: 4 },\\n167|      { n: 2, t0: 4.3, t1: 8 },\\n168|      { n: 5, t0: 8.3, t1: 12 },\\n169|    ],\\n170|  };\\n171|  it(\\\"spans the first to the last chunk in range\\\", () => {\\n172|    expect(sceneSpan(narration, 1, 2)).toEqual({ startSec: 0, endSec: 8 });\\n173|    expect(sceneSpan(narration, 2, 4)).toEqual({ startSec: 4.3, endSec: 8 });\\n174|    expect(sceneSpan(narration, 3, 4)).toBeNull();\\n175|  });\\n176|});\\n177|\\n178|describe(\\\"chaptersToPrepare\\\", () => {\\n179|  it(\\\"follows the owner's rolling window\\\", () => {\\n180|    expect(chaptersToPrepare(\\\"upload\\\", 1, 24)).toEqual([1, 2]);\\n181|    expect(chaptersToPrepare(\\\"enter\\\", 5, 24)).toEqual([6, 7]);\\n182|    expect(chaptersToPrepare(\\\"jump\\\", 5, 24)).toEqual([5, 6]);\\n183|    expect(chaptersToPrepare(\\\"enter\\\", 24, 24)).toEqual([]);\\n184|    expect(chaptersToPrepare(\\\"jump\\\", 24, 24)).toEqual([24]);\\n185|    expect(chaptersToPrepare(\\\"upload\\\", 1, 1)).toEqual([1]);\\n186|  });\\n187|});\\n188|\\n189|describe(\\\"cost\\\", () => {\\n190|  it(\\\"estimates an average Oz chapter near USD 0.003 warm\\\", () => {\\n191|    // ~9,000 chars ≈ 10 min of audio: 9000/15*0.02+8 = 20 s GPU.\\n192|    const micro = estimateNarrationMicro(9000);\\n193|    expect(micro).toBe(Math.ceil(20 * 0.000222 * 1e6));\\n194|    expect(micro / 1e6).toBeCloseTo(0.0044, 3);\\n195|    expect(actualNarrationMicro(7.1)).toBe(Math.ceil(7.1 * 0.000222 * 1e6));\\n196|    expect(Number.isInteger(estimateNarrationMicro(0))).toBe(true);\\n197|  });\\n198|});\"}}\nagent-logs/40-review-1.jsonl:179:{\"schema_version\":1,\"id\":\"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4b1\",\"stream\":{\"kind\":\"session\",\"id\":\"01a18303-8a86-7fb0-9538-954ee31908b3\"},\"sequence\":179,\"recorded_at\":1780531400000353,\"record_type\":\"event\",\"durability\":\"durable\",\"causation_id\":\"01a18303-8c7e-7df2-afb2-bf2baeb933e8\",\"payload_type\":\"task.lifecycle.output\",\"payload_schema_version\":1,\"payload\":{\"command_id\":\"01a18303-8c7e-7df2-afb2-bf2baeb933e8\",\"event\":{\"chunk\":\"Read text file `docs/contracts/narration.md`.\\n1|# Narration\\n2|\\n3|Read-aloud narration, one compact mp3 per chapter plus a per-chapter\\n4|manifest with sentence timings. The unit is the chapter (owner\\n5|decision): the reader plays any scene by seeking to its first sentence\\n6|(`sceneSpan`) and highlights the sentence being read (`activeChunkAt`).\\n7|Voice Kokoro-82M `af_heart` at speed 0.95, generated on a Modal GPU\\n8|function that scales to zero.\\n9|\\n10|## Manifest\\n11|\\n12|`ChapterNarration` in `core/narration.ts`: `format: 1`, `key`, `src`,\\n13|`durationSec`, `voice`, `model`, `speed`, and `chunks` with `n`\\n14|(paragraph ordinal), `start`/`end` (char offsets into the paragraph),\\n15|and `t0`/`t1` (seconds). `parseChapterNarration` throws on any bad\\n16|field: it is a trust boundary, since the reader fetches this JSON.\\n17|`src` is an `https:` URL or a same-origin path under `/narration/`.\\n18|\\n19|## Cache key\\n20|\\n21|`narrationKeyInput` builds a canonical string from the\\n22|NFC-normalized, whitespace-collapsed chunk texts joined with `\\\"\\\\n\\\"`,\\n23|plus voice, model, speed, and format. Callers hash it with SHA-256;\\n24|`narrationKey` returns `narration/v1/<voice>/<first 32 hex>`. Same\\n25|text + voice + model + speed gives the same key, any edit gives a new\\n26|one. Audio lives at `<key>.mp3`, the manifest at `<key>.json`, as\\n27|deterministic public Blob paths; the Redis index `narr:idx:<key>`\\n28|holds the manifest JSON. Oz is pregenerated through the same keys, so\\n29|a second reader of the same text gets it free.\\n30|\\n31|## Concurrency\\n32|\\n33|One reusable function, `ensureChapterNarration` in\\n34|`core/narration-cache.ts`, serves the offline Oz run and the future\\n35|upload route: index hit, then store hit with index backfill, then lock\\n36|`narr:lock:<key>` (TTL 300 s, `setNxEx`; a null acquire means\\n37|`pending`), one index re-check, budget reserve, synthesize, put audio\\n38|and manifest, index set, release. Cache hits never touch the lock or\\n39|the budget; failures refund once and release. No error text leaves the\\n40|function.\\n41|\\n42|## Spend\\n43|\\n44|Integer micro-dollars. `estimateNarrationMicro(chars)` reserves the\\n45|cap before generating: about 15 chars of audio per second, GPU time\\n46|about 2% of audio after encode, plus 8 s of cold start/overhead, at\\n47|the Modal L4 rate (`KOKORO_L4_USD_PER_SEC`, about USD 0.80/h). The\\n48|server reserves on both the global spend key and the daily spend key\\n49|(`spendKey()`, `dailySpendKey(day)` from `core/images`), refunding\\n50|both past either cap; the global `DAILY_SPEND_CAP_USD` applies. The\\n51|offline run caps with `NARRATION_CAP_USD` (default 2) and stops with a\\n52|report instead of spending more. Worked number: an average Oz chapter\\n53|of ~9,000 chars is about 10 min of audio, about 20 s of warm GPU,\\n54|about USD 0.004.\\n55|\\n56|## Rolling window\\n57|\\n58|The owner warms two chapters ahead: at upload, chapters 1 and 2 while\\n59|the book is processed; entering chapter N ensures N+1 and N+2; jumping\\n60|to N ensures N and N+1. `chaptersToPrepare` in `core/narration.ts`\\n61|computes the window; the client asks, the server dedupes through the\\n62|index and lock.\\n63|\\n64|## Cold start\\n65|\\n66|About 15–30 s for the first chapter after the function scaled to zero\\n67|(`scaledown_window=60`), warm calls a few seconds per chapter. The\\n68|2-ahead window hides it after chapter 1. While a chapter is pending,\\n69|the Read aloud control shows a quiet \\\"Getting the voice ready…\\\"\\n70|state.\\n71|\\n72|## Operations\\n73|\\n74|Deploy with `modal deploy pipeline/modal/narrate.py`; the app\\n75|`lectoria-narration` scales to zero a minute after the last call, and\\n76|`modal app stop lectoria-narration` removes it entirely.\\n77|\\n78|## Open items\\n79|\\n80|Upload route wiring (uses `server/narration/cache.ts`, no route yet);\\n81|Blob vs `public/` for Oz (same keys either way, so switching is a\\n82|re-run).\",\"final_result\":true,\"kind\":\"output\",\"task_id\":\"01a18303-cb67-74f0-a19c-1efa0a26a3e5\"},\"kind\":\"task_lifecycle\",\"run_stream\":{\"id\":\"01a18303-8c7e-7df2-afb2-bf2baeb933e8\",\"kind\":\"run\"},\"task_id\":\"01a18303-cb67-74f0-a19c-1efa0a26a3e5\",\"task_stream\":{\"id\":\"01a18303-cb67-74f0-a19c-1efa0a26a3e5\",\"kind\":\"task\"}}}\nagent-logs/40-review-1.jsonl:184:{\"schema_version\":1,\"id\":\"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4bb\",\"stream\":{\"kind\":\"session\",\"id\":\"01a18303-8a86-7fb0-9538-954ee31908b3\"},\"sequence\":184,\"recorded_at\":1780531400000363,\"record_type\":\"event\",\"durability\":\"durable\",\"causation_id\":\"01a18303-8c7e-7df2-afb2-bf2baeb933e8\",\"payload_type\":\"tool.result\",\"payload_schema_version\":1,\"payload\":{\"call_id\":\"call_01a18303c97e70f9a0c212b2f65637ce\",\"command_id\":\"01a18303-8c7e-7df2-afb2-bf2baeb933e8\",\"correlation_facts\":{\"outcome\":\"success\",\"tool_name\":\"read_file\"},\"kind\":\"tool_result\",\"run_stream\":{\"id\":\"01a18303-8c7e-7df2-afb2-bf2baeb933e8\",\"kind\":\"run\"},\"text\":\"Read text file `docs/contracts/narration.md`.\\n1|# Narration\\n2|\\n3|Read-aloud narration, one compact mp3 per chapter plus a per-chapter\\n4|manifest with sentence timings. The unit is the chapter (owner\\n5|decision): the reader plays any scene by seeking to its first sentence\\n6|(`sceneSpan`) and highlights the sentence being read (`activeChunkAt`).\\n7|Voice Kokoro-82M `af_heart` at speed 0.95, generated on a Modal GPU\\n8|function that scales to zero.\\n9|\\n10|## Manifest\\n11|\\n12|`ChapterNarration` in `core/narration.ts`: `format: 1`, `key`, `src`,\\n13|`durationSec`, `voice`, `model`, `speed`, and `chunks` with `n`\\n14|(paragraph ordinal), `start`/`end` (char offsets into the paragraph),\\n15|and `t0`/`t1` (seconds). `parseChapterNarration` throws on any bad\\n16|field: it is a trust boundary, since the reader fetches this JSON.\\n17|`src` is an `https:` URL or a same-origin path under `/narration/`.\\n18|\\n19|## Cache key\\n20|\\n21|`narrationKeyInput` builds a canonical string from the\\n22|NFC-normalized, whitespace-collapsed chunk texts joined with `\\\"\\\\n\\\"`,\\n23|plus voice, model, speed, and format. Callers hash it with SHA-256;\\n24|`narrationKey` returns `narration/v1/<voice>/<first 32 hex>`. Same\\n25|text + voice + model + speed gives the same key, any edit gives a new\\n26|one. Audio lives at `<key>.mp3`, the manifest at `<key>.json`, as\\n27|deterministic public Blob paths; the Redis index `narr:idx:<key>`\\n28|holds the manifest JSON. Oz is pregenerated through the same keys, so\\n29|a second reader of the same text gets it free.\\n30|\\n31|## Concurrency\\n32|\\n33|One reusable function, `ensureChapterNarration` in\\n34|`core/narration-cache.ts`, serves the offline Oz run and the future\\n35|upload route: index hit, then store hit with index backfill, then lock\\n36|`narr:lock:<key>` (TTL 300 s, `setNxEx`; a null acquire means\\n37|`pending`), one index re-check, budget reserve, synthesize, put audio\\n38|and manifest, index set, release. Cache hits never touch the lock or\\n39|the budget; failures refund once and release. No error text leaves the\\n40|function.\\n41|\\n42|## Spend\\n43|\\n44|Integer micro-dollars. `estimateNarrationMicro(chars)` reserves the\\n45|cap before generating: about 15 chars of audio per second, GPU time\\n46|about 2% of audio after encode, plus 8 s of cold start/overhead, at\\n47|the Modal L4 rate (`KOKORO_L4_USD_PER_SEC`, about USD 0.80/h). The\\n48|server reserves on both the global spend key and the daily spend key\\n49|(`spendKey()`, `dailySpendKey(day)` from `core/images`), refunding\\n50|both past either cap; the global `DAILY_SPEND_CAP_USD` applies. The\\n51|offline run caps with `NARRATION_CAP_USD` (default 2) and stops with a\\n52|report instead of spending more. Worked number: an average Oz chapter\\n53|of ~9,000 chars is about 10 min of audio, about 20 s of warm GPU,\\n54|about USD 0.004.\\n55|\\n56|## Rolling window\\n57|\\n58|The owner warms two chapters ahead: at upload, chapters 1 and 2 while\\n59|the book is processed; entering chapter N ensures N+1 and N+2; jumping\\n60|to N ensures N and N+1. `chaptersToPrepare` in `core/narration.ts`\\n61|computes the window; the client asks, the server dedupes through the\\n62|index and lock.\\n63|\\n64|## Cold start\\n65|\\n66|About 15–30 s for the first chapter after the function scaled to zero\\n67|(`scaledown_window=60`\n[tool output bounded: strategy=head, original_bytes=174748, visible_bytes=10000